#                                  # vanished-file sweep only on a complete pass, no branch/sha in the state) and drops the
#                                  # "index of <branch>@<sha7>, synced <age> ago" line on search_code_semantic results
# CODE_INDEX_STALE_BASE_GUARD_DISABLED=1  # code-index stale-base gate (2026-10-23): restores the pre-fix behaviour — every checkout a
#                                  # sync reads may update AND delete the shared project index rows, however old its base is
#                                  # (a month-old lane worktree's complete listing purges newer files' rows; refusals carry
#                                  # refused:true on index_swept and "FROZEN" on the search freshness line)
#                                             # step is a wait lane and never takes this path; fixer 2026-09-27) no longer gets the appended
#                                             # '[ALL-COMPLETE BOARD — harness-verified at fire time …]' advisory nor the
#                                             # loop_metrics schedule_allcomplete_firing row { scheduleId, steps, planUnchangedSinceLastFire, action }
#                                             # board is unchanged since the last firing AND the last firing is < 6 h old (heartbeat floor);
#                                             # SCHEDULE_ALL_COMPLETE_SKIP_DISABLED=1 turns the skip off again even when enabled
#                                             # OWNER-ARMED schedule (promptSetBy user / legacy null) — observe-only either way (fixer 2026-09-27:
#                                             # AUDIT_CHURN_RULE scopes "lengthen its cadence" to machine-armed rows and schedule_get prints "armed by")

#                                  # the lane's p50 run length × SCHEDULE_DURATION_FIT_MULTIPLIER (its last 10 FINISHED
#                                  # agent_runs) is NOT stretched — the requested cadence lands as typed again (pre-B3: 15-min
#                                  # rows armed on 546–991-min lanes fired 0× and only busy-skipped). Unset = createSchedule/
#                                  # updateScheduleForUser stretch it to ≥ multiplier × p50 (rounded up to 5 min, ≥15 min,
#                                  # ≤ 1 day), the tool response says so (⏱ CADENCE STRETCHED + stretchedFrom), owner-armed
#                                  # cadences are only advised, and ONE loop_metrics schedule_duration_fit row { outcome:
#                                  # stretched|warned, requestedSec, intervalSec, floorSec, p50RunMs, samples, multiplier } is
#                                  # written. <3 finished runs or a read error = no change.
# SCHEDULE_DURATION_FIT_MULTIPLIER=1 # fixer pass on B3 (2026-09-27): the cadence-floor multiplier (finite, > 0, clamped at 10).
#                                  # Default 1 — the branch's 2× halved the steady-state duty cycle of every machine lane whose
#                                  # run exceeds half its cadence (idle ≈ p50 between firings, against the 2026-09-11 "full
#                                  # steam" rule); at 1× a busy-skip occurs only on an above-median run and clears within the
#                                  # sweeper's +3-min retry. Set 2 to restore the branch's spacing. Junk = default.
# SCHEDULE_DURATION_FIT_FIRST_FIRING_STRETCHED=1 # fixer pass on B3: a stretched arm's FIRST firing waits the full stretched
#                                  # interval (the branch shape). Unset = the stretch is a recurrence change only — the first
#                                  # nextRunAt keeps the REQUESTED delay (a lane ending its run with `schedule_self recurring
#                                  # 15 min` is picked up in 15 min when idle; a busy lane rides the +3-min busy-skip retry), and
#                                  # the sweeper's post-fire claim re-arms at the stretched intervalSec from then on.
# SCHEDULE_DURATION_FIT_COLLAPSE_STRETCHED=1 # fixer pass on B3: a stretched arm still runs the ae20da66 same-cadence collapse at
#                                  # the STRETCHED interval (the branch shape — which cancelled a DIFFERENT sub-floor job: 15-
#                                  # and 30-min arms on a 600-min lane both land at the floor). Unset = a stretched arm never
#                                  # collapses (superseded empty; the 1ead3b52 identical-prompt dedup still adopts).
# SCHEDULE_DURATION_DEADLINE_ENABLED=1 # OPT-IN (finding B3, 2026-09-27): a run FIRED BY a recurring machine/system schedule
#                                  # gets a soft deadline of max(20 min, 3× the schedule's interval) through the v1#33
#                                  # AgentProfile.runDeadlineMs seam (tools-off final, never a kill; RUN_DEADLINE_ENABLED, when
#                                  # set, wins). Unset = no deadline — the 2026-09-11 gate flip stands (0.8× cadence truncated
#                                  # 11.3% of machine runs). Owner-armed rows and one-shots never carry it.

# PREMISE_REVISION_DISABLED=1      # premise register finding C3 (2026-09-27): restores the SILENT goal_premise_set merge —
#                                  # no prevValue/prevManifest/revisedAt stamps, no premise_revised loop_metrics row, no
#                                  # premiseRevisions[] on the answer, no PREMISE REVISIONS section / manifest tags / like-for-like
#                                  # gap lines on the project [BOARD], and the hourly [PREMISE CONFLICT] check groups by key only
#                                  # again (manifests ignored; no observe-only 'not_like_for_like' row). Unset = a beyond-tolerance
#                                  # re-registration is named everywhere; on the board the C3 lines sit inside the shrink ladder
#                                  # (review fix 2026-09-27: OWNER QUESTIONS are never cut where the OFF rendering keeps them),
#                                  # an unset manifest is a wildcard in the conflict check, and a manifest is sanitized, never refused.
# GOAL_CONTINUE_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 # agent-decisions prerequisite 6 (2026-09-27): no goal_continue loop_metrics row per goal-continue
#                                  # evaluation { round, progressed, stalls, evidenceToolCalls, unfinished, resumed } and terminal runs NULL
#                                  # agent_runs.checkpoint again. Unset = the row is written and a terminal finalize keeps a TRIMMED
#                                  # ≤ 4 KB summary (counters + plan step STATES, no transcript, terminal:true — never resumable).
#                                  # sinceCloseMs, withinWindow}) when a done goal LEAVES 'done' (goal_update seam 'update' or the
#                                  # todo-driven auto-reopen seam 'auto'). The reopen itself always lands. GOAL_DONE_SUSPECT_DISABLED
#                                  # silences it too.
#                                  # that is not a drift ("(observed 5.33tok/s, manual)" for a goal_premise_set observed) — drift-only again.
#                                  # same-project directive still names is NOT badged '⚠ suspect: open_directive' (close-time only again).
#                                  # 40 with BOTH halves of a "<goal> · <step>" title kept.
#                                  # doneSuspect tool-result note when a goal closes 'done' with its own target_* premise unmet
#                                  # (observed value under the bar), a HOLD progress note, or an open owner directive naming it; no
#                                  # '⚠ suspect' badge on the [BOARD] goal line or the fleet roll-up. A target premise NEVER observed
#                                  # is telemetry only (reason premise_target_unobserved — no badge, no reopen instruction; review fix
#                                  # 2026-09-27). The close itself is NEVER refused either way.
#                                  # last 7 days too (stamp only — no drift wake, no conflict flag) so a '⚠ suspect' close clears
#                                  # itself once its source meets the bar. =1 restores the active/blocked-only scan byte-for-byte.

#                                  # `once` arm from a schedule firing on its OWN chat is stamped chainedFromScheduleId; a chain of
#                                  # ≥3 links in a rolling 24h is governed as a RECURRING cadence — cap-cadence math on the OBSERVED
#                                  # cadence at arm time (can-never-fit ⇒ CAP MATH warning by default; ≥75% ⇒ CAP HEADROOM warning),
#                                  # dedupe against an enabled recurring twin, a loud advisory on the arm response, a fire-time
#                                  # dormancy check (observe-only by default), busy re-arm + busySkips instead of queue-behind-busy.
#                                  # Set = the stamp and the loop_metrics schedule_once_chain rows STAY (telemetry never gated) but
#                                  # no link is ever classified recurring-like; every reader fails open.
#                                  # chain link whose OBSERVED cadence can never fit the daily cap is REFUSED at arm time like a
#                                  # recurring machine arm (metric outcome refused_cap_cadence). Unset = it lands with the ⚠️ CAP MATH
#                                  # warning and a warned_cap_cadence { wouldRefuse:true } row.
#                                  # (enabled:false, 'parked:dormant', metric parked_dormant) — a parked one-shot never re-arms itself;
#                                  # only resume_schedule once live work exists revives it. Unset = the sweeper records
#                                  # would_park_dormant and the link FIRES (observe-only).
