# Worker DRAIN on deploy (owner 2026-09-24: "why is it waiting 24 minutes for a
# question?" — every deploy wave docker-stopped box C's worker after 45 s,
# interrupting 2–4 runs per wave; the owner's own turn queued behind the churn).
# Now SIGTERM = drain: no new claims, active runs finish in place, the process
# exits when idle; deploy-coding-worker.sh sends the signal and does NOT wait.
# WORKER_DRAIN_MAX_MS=21600000                     # drain bound (6 h since 2026-09-25; was 2 h): runs still active past it are interrupted (checkpoints retained)
# DRAIN_YIELD_AFTER_MS=1500000                     # soft yield (2026-10-19): after this long in drain, ask still-active runs to hand off at their next step boundary (default 25 min); the hard bound above stays
# DRAIN_YIELD_DISABLED=1                           # restore finish-in-place (no soft yield)
# Drainer PARKING (deploy-coding-worker.sh, operator iteration 12, 2026-09-25): a
# previous wave's still-draining worker is renamed out of the way and the new
# worker starts in a per-wave compose project, so no deploy ever stops a
# draining worker for its color. Beyond WORKER_MAX_DRAINERS parked drainers the
# oldest is interrupted. WORKER_DRAIN_PARK_DISABLED=1 restores the bounded wait.
# WORKER_MAX_DRAINERS=4
# WORKER_DRAIN_PARK_DISABLED=1
# Deploy BATCHING (ticket ed057f9d, 2026-10-16): the drainer cap used to evict
# a drainer with LIVE runs the moment a rebuild needed its slot (measured
# 2026-10-16: 4/4 slots busy, oldest 99 min into a 7-run drain). Two levers,
# both in deploy-coding-worker.sh (kill-switched, on-box only):
#   1) WORKER_DRAIN_SLOT_WAIT_MAX_SEC (600): before parking a new drainer when
#      the pool is full, evict run-FREE parked drainers immediately, then WAIT
#      (bounded) for a live one to exit; only past the bound does the cap
#      eviction fire. 600 not 900+: the wait runs inside the Deploy job whose
#      updated_at freezes at job start — deploy-watchdog.sh arm 1 cancels at
#      90 min. WORKER_DRAIN_SLOT_WAIT_DISABLED=1 restores instant eviction.
#   2) WORKER_ROLLOUT_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC (1800): at most one box-C worker
#      rollout per window — a wave whose inputs changed but whose last rollout
#      is younger defers the rebuild to the next wave (no stamp write; the
#      pending hash ages and WORKER_ROLLOUT_MAX_STALE_SEC (7200) forces a
#      rollout when a burst would otherwise starve it forever). A deferred
#      worker honestly reports its build sha (classifyWorkerLag "real", by
#      design, bounded by the window). WORKER_ROLLOUT_WINDOW_DISABLED=1
#      restores every-wave rollout (also the manual force-roll override).
# WORKER_DRAIN_SLOT_WAIT_MAX_SEC=600
# WORKER_DRAIN_SLOT_POLL_SEC=30
# WORKER_ROLLOUT_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC=1800
# WORKER_ROLLOUT_MAX_STALE_SEC=7200
# Goal/todo READ tools (goal_get / todo_get) also resolve a unique exact TITLE
# (case-insensitive) among the caller's visible rows (iteration 12). Set to 1
# to restore id-only resolution.
# Utility thinking leg (operator iteration 13, 2026-09-25): opt-in thinking
# calls send reasoning_effort (low|high|max; 'off' omits — default low: at the
# vendor default V4.1 Flash reasoned 50k+ chars and answered EMPTY), and a
# budget-exhausted empty answer (finish_reason=length) is retried ONCE with
# thinking off on the same model before the DashScope fallback.
# UTILITY_THINKING_EFFORT=low
# FO firing 47 (2026-09-29): the 'utility' role override latch escalates its
# backoff window 5→15→30→60 min while the custom utility seat stays
# unreachable (prod: a sustained slowdown re-paid the full 30s caller timeout
# every 5 min for 4h). =1 restores the old flat 5-min window.
# DELETED 2026-10-30 (RSW-1 delete-with-ledger cluster 12, goal 393f731e): was
#   CLOCK_SCHEDULE_HAYSTACK_DISABLED=1 - NF_INERT (0 compose/Dockerfile hits), reader removed; the
#   machine-wake clock guard ALWAYS counts the owner's enabled schedule fire times
#   (scheduleClockHaystack) as quoted forward data, so a supervisor citing "morning nudge 7:31 AM PDT"
#   is not struck (it still fails open to [] on any DB error).
# Unified-memory semantic leg: minimum embedding timeout in ms (default 1200; was 800 — DashScope wobble tripped it).
# UNIFIED_MEMORY_EMBED_MIN_TIMEOUT_MS=1200
# Finish long supervisor wakes in place across deploys (WI-G, 2026-09-25): the
# web colour's blue-green drain cut a glm-5.3 reasoning-max supervisor wake
# (8–16 min) ~3×/day at the 900 s retiring budget (chat_run_interrupted
# reason=deploy). Backend side (default ON): /drain-status reports per-run
# {runId, chatId, startedAt, isSupervisorWake, lastToolAt} + extensionEligible;
# a MACHINE chat run on a RETIRING colour gets ONE harness notice at its next
# tool round ("torn down in ~N s — write your final now"; loop_metric
# deploy_retire_nudge); fleet-telemetry view 'deploy' carries deployInterrupts24h.
# DEPLOY_RETIRE_BUDGET_SECONDS=900                 # what the nudge assumes the deploy's retiring budget is (mirror DRAIN_MAX_RETIRING_SECONDS)
# DRAIN_PROGRESS_WINDOW_SECONDS=120                # a run counts as progressing when its last tool call is at most this old
# Deploy-script side (runner env, NOT the container — see deploy-blue-green.sh;
# DEFAULT OFF = byte-identical drain): DRAIN_RETIRING_EXTENSION_SECONDS=600
# extends the retiring budget ONCE when every remaining run is a progressing
# supervisor wake, capped by DRAIN_RETIRING_TOTAL_CAP_SECONDS=1500.
# (2026-10-20, deep research has no wall clock) DRAIN_RESEARCH_EXTENSION_SECONDS=600
# (DEFAULT ON, research-only) extends it ONCE when /drain-status says
# "researchExtensionEligible":true — a deep-research council on the old colour is
# still PROGRESSING (a model / tool event inside COUNCIL_STALL_MS) and every other
# run is a progressing council or supervisor wake; same cap; no research run in
# flight = byte-identical drain; =0 turns it off (set it as the GitHub repo
# Variable DRAIN_RESEARCH_EXTENSION_SECONDS — deploy.yml forwards it to the box),
# and the backend's RESEARCH_NO_WALL_CLOCK_DISABLED=1 reports the flag false.
# WORKER_DRAIN_FILE=/tmp/worker-draining           # marker the deploy script reads (docker exec test -f) to exclude a draining worker from color detection
# WORKER_DRAIN_ON_DEPLOY_DISABLED=1                # kill switch (deploy side): retire the old worker with docker stop -t 45 as before
# WORKER_DRAIN_WAIT_MAX_SEC=900                    # deploy side: how long a same-color deploy waits for a still-draining container before interrupting it
# Deploy-speed switches (2026-09-26 wave anatomy — deploy_speedups #1/#2/#3/#5/#6/#8).
# RUNNER env: GitHub repo Variables (`gh variable set NAME --body VALUE`) that
# deploy.yml forwards to deploy-blue-green.sh / prebuild-inactive.sh; unset =
# the default shown. Pinned by scripts/deploy/blue-green-speedups.test.sh;
# runbook docs/REMOTE_OPS.md "Deploy tuning switches".
# BUILDER_CACHE_KEEP=40GB                          # #1 BuildKit cache kept by the ONE post-build prune (10GB evicted every wave's layers → 9-min from-scratch builds)
# BUILDER_PRUNE_ONCE_DISABLED=1                    # #8 re-add the second (end-of-deploy) builder prune
# DRAIN_SECONDS=10                                 # #8 SSE-grace floor before the /drain-status poll (was 60; 60 restores)
# WORKER_IMAGE_SHARED_DISABLED=1                   # #5 build the worker image separately again (default: worker runs the backend tag, like relay)
# BACKEND_CHOWN_RECURSIVE=1                        # #2 restore `chown -R nodejs:nodejs /app` in backend/Dockerfile (compose build arg; also honoured from the box .env)
# FRONTEND_CONTENT_BUST=1                          # #6 DEFAULT OFF: bust the frontend build on sha256(frontend/) (scripts/deploy/frontend-bust-key.sh) — same rsync'd tree on every box ⇒ parity kept; DEPLOY_SHA stays the runtime env
# PREBUILD_STATELESS=1                             # #3 DEFAULT OFF: pre-build the stateless boxes' inactive colour in the background while host 1 deploys (scripts/deploy/prebuild-inactive.sh; compose build only)
# PREBUILD_STATELESS_DISABLED=1                    # #3 kill switch (also honoured by the script itself)
# MIGRATE_LOCK_RECOVERY_DISABLED=1                 # 2026-10-22 (1 / true / on): box A runs ONE `prisma migrate deploy` — no resolve + retry of a lost lock wait of an
#                                                 # atomic in-place lock-retry migration, no P3009 probe (scripts/deploy/migrate-lock-recovery.sh). A repo Variable
#                                                 # deploy.yml forwards over the Blue-green step's stdin script, or a line in box A's
#                                                 # /opt/crossmodel-local/deploy-flags.env; runbook docs/REMOTE_OPS.md "A migration failed: P3009 / P3018".
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_MAX_ACTIVE_WORKERS=   # concurrent active children per PROJECT SUPERVISOR (every project) — the explicit
#                                                 # operator override; forwarded to backend + worker since 2026-10-20 (before that it reached
#                                                 # neither). Unset = the coding worker's LIVE machine-claimable slots from the Redis slot
#                                                 # registry (coding/worker-slots.ts: CODING_WORKER_CONCURRENCY − the 1-slot interactive
#                                                 # reserve; box C 32 → 31; newest entry per BOX_NAME, boxes summed, entries > 90 s stale
#                                                 # ignored), else this process's own CODING_WORKER_CONCURRENCY − 1 (only inside a worker
#                                                 # with slots), else 24. A refusal at the ceiling writes ONE project_supervisor_breaker
#                                                 # row reason 'concurrency' {activeCount, cap, capSource: env|live|process|default}.
# WORKER_SLOT_REGISTRY_DISABLED=1                # 2026-10-20 release switch: the worker publishes no slot entry and the ceiling skips the
#                                                 # live read (env / process / 24 only — the pre-2026-10-20 behaviour)
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_SPAWNS_PER_HOUR=32     # rolling hourly spawn rate per project supervisor (OBSERVE-ONLY unless RATE_ENFORCE=1); this and the two STORM numbers below are forwarded to backend + worker since 2026-10-20
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_STORM_MAX_SPAWNS_10MIN=12 # runaway detector: more allowed spawns than this in
#                                                 # 10 min records project_supervisor_breaker + an advisory
#                                                 # line (OBSERVE-ONLY since 2026-09-14)
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_STORM_ENFORCE=1        # opt-in: the storm breaker REFUSES spawns for the cooldown
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_RATE_ENFORCE=1         # opt-in: the hourly spawn-rate cap REFUSES (default: observe-only advisory + project_supervisor_breaker metric reason 'rate')
# DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_STORM_COOLDOWN_SEC=1800 # breaker cooldown
# (DIGBY_PROJECT_SUPERVISOR_DAILY_BUDGET_USD — DELETED 2026-09-27 with the spawn "token-budget
#  circuit breaker": a spawn is never refused on cost; no hidden cost caps — owner directive.)
# Memory unification (owner 2026-09-14: "project level memory and embed and rerank
# read write for coding sessions" + "per user gates"). All default ON; every read of
# the unified store / knowledge base is scoped to projects the caller owns or is a
# member of (folder inheritance), blends only over OWNED projects (memory/memory-access.ts):
# CODING_PROJECT_MEMORY_INJECT_DISABLED=1   # coding run start: skip the [PROJECT MEMORY] block
#                                           # (learnings + decisions + knowledge-base chunks, ≤3500 chars)
# CODING_MEMORY_PIPELINE_DISABLED=1         # coding finalize: don't run the project-state extractor
# CODING_HUMAN_TURN_MEMORY_DISABLED=1       # coding finalize: treat HUMAN-typed session turns as machine runs again (no personal-fact extraction; 2026-09-21 default = human turns feed personal memory like a chat)
#   (the same switch also turns reasoning off for the nightly coding-project dream; 2026-09-22: it had failed every night — a 600-token budget truncated its JSON)
# PROFILE_FIELD_CAPS_DISABLED=1             # 2026-10-20 release switch (memory/profile-guard.ts): the user-profile extractor shows the model
#                                           # an UNBOUNDED stored profile, sends the old "summary (1 line)" field line and saves whatever
#                                           # parses. Default ON = each field capped (summary 300 / preferences 500 / currentFocus 200 /
#                                           # communicationStyle 300 chars / 5 topics × 80), shown clamped, saved clamped — the whole-profile
#                                           # echo always fits the 1800-token budget (the profile parse_error bursts: an accreted profile
#                                           # cut inside its first field never saved, so it never shrank)
# PROFILE_EXTRACT_THROTTLE_DISABLED=1       # 2026-10-20 release switch: one profile extraction per eligible turn again. Default ON = one
#                                           # per user in flight, then 60 s (15 min after a parse/LLM failure) — in-process, per backend;
#                                           # explicit rejections bypass it and a throttled turn still extracts its flat facts. The next
#                                           # profile memory_extraction row carries meta.throttledSkips
# MEMORY_STATE_OPS_DISABLED=1               # 2026-10-20 release switch (memory/state-ops.ts): every structured memory writer —
#                                           # profile / project / thread extractors, coding fold + dream + user prefs, the user
#                                           # dream — goes back to asking the model to RE-EMIT the whole stored object. Default ON =
#                                           # per-item ops: the model sees the state with an [id] per item and answers only the
#                                           # change (set / add / update / remove / put, or {}), so the answer is bounded by the
#                                           # change, not by the size of the stored memory (the echo is what outgrew every budget)
# FACT_VERSIONS_DISABLED=1                  # 2026-10-20 release switch (memory/fact-versions.ts): no user_memory_fact_versions
#                                           # reads or writes and no "(since …)" dates in the extraction / dream prompts. Default ON =
#                                           # a changed fact is closed with replacedBy + a new open version (timestamps, source chat);
#                                           # a user-intent forget / clear purges the history
# MEMORY_ARCHIVE_DISABLED=1                 # 2026-10-20 release switch (memory/memory-archive.ts): a full digby_memory scope DELETES
#                                           # its evicted rows again. Default ON = they MOVE to digby_memory_archive (text only, FTS),
#                                           # read only by the search_memory tool as an [archived] top-up; retention 30 d session /
# ADMIN_DELETE_PROTECTED_EMAILS             # 2026-10-27 (ticket 054daeb7): comma-separated emails adminDeleteUser REFUSES to hard-
#                                           # delete — default 'claudebot@digby.ai', the canonical deploy-smoke account the auth
#                                           # smoke gate logs in as on every wave (owner deleted it 04:13:43Z; deploys went red for
#                                           # hours). Empty string = unprotected (the documented override).
#                                           # 365 d other (daily memory-archive-retention cron); explicit deletions purge both tiers
# DREAM_ALL_ACTIVE_USERS_DISABLED=1         # 2026-10-20 release switch: the user memory dream goes back to a 20 h global lock and at
#                                           # most 30 users per cycle. Default ON = an hourly tick dreams every eligible user (changed
#                                           # since their last dream, last dream >= 20 h ago) until the 12-min tick deadline
# LEARNINGS_DREAM_DISABLED=1                # 2026-10-20 ops switch: stop the daily learnings-dream cron (coding/learnings-dream.ts),
#                                           # which merges near-duplicate entries in each project's LEARNINGS INDEX (never the repo
#                                           # file) — <= 30 % absorbed per pass, each project at most every 7 days
# DREAM_OPS_LENGTH_RETRY_DISABLED=1         # 2026-10-21 release switch (memory-maintenance.service.ts): a finishReason=length clip on
#                                           # a dream-ops answer goes back to a single 1500-token attempt (no 4000-token retry,
#                                           # no dream_ops_length_retry metric). Default ON = the clipped answer is retried ONCE at
#                                           # DREAM_OPS_LENGTH_RETRY_BUDGET_TOKENS (4000) so a merge-heavy consolidation parses.
#                                           # run_spend row via a shared per-turn ledger (chat-agent/turn-spend.ts; meta.seats labels the split).
#                                           # Set to restore the pre-WI-D shape: each loop keeps its own accumulator and only the lead's
#                                           # top-level loops write run_spend (the checker/council meter $0 again; retries mint extra rows).
#                                           # pick via set_chat_mode {leadModel}); every chat runs the instance seat again. Writes still persist.
# MACHINE_TURN_CROSSCHECK_ENABLED=1        # Level 2: run the Double Checker on hook/agent-origin machine turns again (2026-09-22 owner default: every machine-origin turn runs the orchestrator alone; human turns keep the checker)
# CHAT_HUMAN_TURN_EFFORT=high             # orchestrator reasoning_effort on HUMAN-typed chat turns (glm/deepseek built-ins): low|medium|high|max — default high (2026-09-22: owner questions took p50 11 min at max); 'max' restores the 2026-09-03 everywhere-max
# PROJECT_STATUS_HOURLY_ENABLED=1           # 2026-09-29: project supervisor chats get the HOURLY card + 'no change' stub again (default: a card ONLY on a milestone change — a session finished/started, a goal/to-do moved, a new question, the KPI, a quarter-mark of progress)
# AGENT_EVENTS_RETENTION_DISABLED=1       # stop the agent_events retention job (owner 2026-09-22: 19 GB / 26.8 M rows > 14 d with no policy)
# AGENT_EVENTS_RETENTION_DRY_RUN=1        # report what one tick WOULD delete, delete nothing
# AGENT_EVENTS_RETENTION_DAYS=30          # hot window (min 7); rows older than this are deleted in bounded PK-range batches
# AGENT_EVENTS_RETENTION_BATCH=5000       # rows per batch; AGENT_EVENTS_RETENTION_MAX_BATCHES=4 batches per 60 s tick (≈ 29 M rows/day capacity)
#                                           # (machineRun) over the accepted final
#                                           # source 'decision' rows in digby_memory
#                                           # sub-block from the knowledge block
# PROJECT_LEARNINGS_TIMEOUT_MS=10000        # 2026-09-28 (backlog audit PE-12): the USER-TURN soft deadline for the
#                                           # learnings lookup (was a fixed 6 s, which dropped the block on ~1 turn
#                                           # in 7 — p95 9.79 s; machine wakes keep the 15 s context deadline). A
#                                           # deadline hit is logged at info + ONE loop_metrics memory_search_timing
#                                           # row {purpose:'project_learnings', phase:'deadline', deadlineMs} — the
#                                           # p95-vs-deadline readout that says whether to move this. Floor 1000.
#                                           # before the enriched-context load (overlapping it) instead of after it
#                                           # inside the RAG section. Set =1 for the pre-2026-09-28 placement.
# DELETED 2026-11-02 (RSW-1 delete-with-ledger, goal 393f731e): was
#                                           # HOOK_IMMEDIATE_DELIVERY_DISABLED=1 (2026-09-14 instant hooks: skip the
#                                           # emission kick + run-end drain). Inert in prod (no compose file forwards it)
#                                           # and its OFF default is the LIVE behavior, so instant delivery is now
#                                           # UNCONDITIONAL — the emission kick + run-end drain always run.
#                                           # redirect wrappers; the pipes/search tools follow ONE hop to the
#                                           # real URL before scraping/citing. Set =1 to keep the wrappers.
# DELETED 2026-10-30 (RSW-1 delete-with-ledger, goal 393f731e): was
#                                           # SERP_PROVIDER_GUARD_DISABLED=1 (2026-10-07, tickets 9b944f30 +
#                                           # ca805a61). The switch was inert in prod (no compose file and no
#                                           # frontend/Dockerfile forwards it), so the guard below could never be
#                                           # turned off in a deployed process and is now UNCONDITIONAL. Retained as
#                                           # behaviour documentation: BrightData's MCP search tier sometimes wraps a
#                                           # provider failure (429 sr_rate_limit / 502 with x-brd-error-code) as a
#                                           # SUCCESSFUL result whose text is the error body linking
#                                           # docs.brightdata.com. The guard classifies the body at the search TIER
#                                           # (mcp-search gateway retries + the callMcpTool chokepoint — EVERY
#                                           # search_engine consumer: the agent-facing tool, news, feed, kid path,
#                                           # moonshot, web_pipe, youtube_pipe) and in web_pipe itself: the body is a
#                                           # FAILED attempt (retry/backoff + circuit breaker, honoring
#                                           # x-brd-rate-limit-period-ms / the 15 s query-ban floor, fail-fast on the
#                                           # deterministic unexpected_q class), callers get the honest null + a failure
#                                           # naming the code — and search-derived links on the provider's own host are
#                                           # dropped (pre- and post-unwrap). GIVEN urls and JSON organic[] result sets
#                                           # are never filtered.
#                                           # WEB_PIPE_SERP_RETRY_MS (default 3000) tunes web_pipe's in-band
#                                           # retry wait.
# HELPER_SEAT_FALLBACK_DISABLED=1           # 2026-09-14: a CUSTOM-endpoint Helper seat that answers 4xx (not
#                                           # 401/403), times out, refuses the connection or returns empty
#                                           # falls back ONCE to the built-in helper for that call, with an
#                                           # honest attribution + loop_metric seat_fallback. Set =1 to fail hard.
#                                           # "hooks" — postEdit [{run, match, timeoutMs}] run after edit_file /
#                                           # write_file ({file} = the path) and report as a [post-edit hook] line;
#                                           # preCommand [{block, message}] refuse a matching run_command with the
#                                           # PROJECT's message (substring or /regex/). The platform adds no rule of
#                                           # its own; no "hooks" section = unchanged. loop_metric repo_hook.
#                                           # busy-skipped ≥ 10 times (the Fleet Supervisor sweep sat at 98 while
#                                           # hook wakes chained through the finalize drain), the run's finalize
#                                           # yields its queue/hook drain ONCE and pulls that schedule to now so the
#                                           # sweep takes the next slot; its log line names it (metric removed by S-2 2026-10-08). Set =1
#                                           # to restore hooks-always-first.
#                                           # bounded re-orchestration now carries the rejected draft (quoted) and
#                                           # this run's tool RESULT texts, so the retry is a rewrite + one fresh
#                                           # read instead of redoing the whole wake (38 retries/day; one took 16
#                                           # min). Metric meta machine_wake_reject_back {seeded, retryMs}. Set =1
#                                           # to restore the notice-only retry.
#                                           # already has ANOTHER run 'running' with leaseExpiresAt > now() — the DB
#                                           # lease (heartbeated every 2.5 min) is the durable per-session mutex behind
#                                           # the evictable Redis run lock. Live: session 82656032 ran three runs at
#                                           # once after allkeys-lru evicted its lock. Set =1 to restore the
#                                           # Redis-lock-only claim.
#                                           # intervalMinutes on a kind:'once' row is a RETIME (nextRunAt = now +
#                                           # interval, kind stays 'once'). The OLD
#                                           # behavior — a silent no-op that stored intervalSec but never moved
#                                           # nextRunAt while the envelope printed "now every N min" — made the
#                                           # CanLaw supervisor think a one-shot had flipped to a recurring
#                                           # 27-min loop and burn 3 cancel+re-arm rows. Set =1 to refuse the
#                                           # retime HONESTLY instead (never the old silent no-op).
# WORKTREE_SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES=393216        # 2026-09-21 (autonomy loop #14): hard ceiling on the SERIALIZED Files-tab
#                                           # worktree snapshot written to Redis (default 384 KB, floor 16 KB). Bodies
#                                           # are dropped largest-first, then the deepest tree entries (truncated:true).
#                                           # 245 uncapped snapshots (238 MB) filled the 256 MB Redis and evicted the
#                                           # run locks. Metric worktree_snapshot_trimmed. TTL is now 7 d (was 30 d).
#                                           # PARKED (enabled:false, parked:dormant) while its account has had no coding
#                                           # run for 7 days and holds no active goal, open todo, live watched resource
#                                           # or enabled recurring schedule on any other chat; ensureFleetSupervisor
#                                           # resumes the parked row on the account's next project/chat/session. Live:
#                                           # four foreign-account supervisors swept dormant accounts — 17 no-op wakes
#                                           # (~$2.8) a day. The wildcard hook stays armed. Metric fleet_sweep_dormancy.
#                                           # nothing ("none", "n/a", "00000000" — 88 refusals in 48 h from five lanes) is
#                                           # applied to the CALLING chat's only enabled machine-authored schedule (the
#                                           # lane's own work; result carries a [SCHEDULE ID NOTE] naming the real id).
#                                           # Otherwise the refusal now lists the caller's schedules. cancel_schedule
#                                           # never substitutes. Metric schedule_id_substituted. Set =1 for the bare refusal.
# DELETED 2026-10-30 (RSW-1 delete-with-ledger cluster 12, goal 393f731e): was
