# ── Computer use: review of the 0.6.1 wave (2026-09-25) ──
# COMPUTER_DEADLINE_INCLUDES_LOCK_WAIT=1   # review #1: the session deadline is RE-BASED once the per-device use-lock is
#                                          # held (a 60 s contended wait no longer eats a 120 s browser_task→computer
#                                          # handoff's budget). =1 restores the pre-lock clock (deadline counted from
#                                          # session start, lock wait included).
#                                          # Agent-side twins (Mac agent ≥0.6.2, set in the agent's environment /
#                                          # launchd plist, NOT here):
#                                          #   DIGBY_CAPTURE_PIXEL_CHECK=off    — skip the captured-PNG pixel-size
#                                          #     re-attribution (review blocking #1: 0.6.1's check compared a number to a
#                                          #     bridged STRING and was inert; 0.6.2 emits numeric backing pixels and
#                                          #     also accepts point size × integer scale; identical panels → "ambiguous",
#                                          #     never re-attributed by guess). Aspect reconciliation still runs.
#                                          #   DIGBY_FRONT_WINDOW_PROBE=off     — skip the System Events frontmost-window
#                                          #     probe (review #2: it is now a SEPARATE parallel osascript capped at 5 s,
#                                          #     so an Automation stall no longer kills the 10 s display-topology read;
#                                          #     off = capture display from pointer → main, no frontmostApp/Window).
#                                          #   DIGBY_REMOTE_SESSION_IGNORE=<kinds|all> — comma list of remote-session
#                                          #     kinds NOT to report (review #3): `virtual_display` (a BetterDisplay /
#                                          #     DeskPad / HDMI-dummy display naming itself "Virtual Display"),
#                                          #     `teamviewer_desktop` (the TeamViewer app merely open),
#                                          #     `screensharingd`, `screen_sharing_virtual_display`, or `all`. Default
#                                          #     empty = every kind counts (0.6.1 behavior) — a headless Mac on a dummy
#                                          #     display otherwise keeps every machine-triggered run camera-only.
#                                           # EXISTING cm:wt-snap:* pile to the byte ceiling and clamps TTLs to 7 d, one
#                                           # pass per 6 h fleet-wide (NX lock). Without it the 244 uncapped snapshots
#                                           # (22–29 d of TTL left at 252 MB / 256 MB) would keep evicting run locks for
#                                           # a month. Metric worktree_snapshot_hygiene (value = bytes freed).
#                                           # schedule firing, hook wake, agent/webhook send, the coding-dispatch heal —
#                                           # is refused with reason 'archived' (never 'busy'); only a real user turn
#                                           # restores an archived chat. Live: lane b95e9df6, archived under the
#                                           # owner's stop order, was revived by a leftover peer hook and burned a
#                                           # derail-killed run. Metric machine_dispatch_archived_refused {surface}.
#                                           # Set =1 to restore the silent un-archive heal.
# FINISHED_CHILD_ARCHIVE_DISABLED=1        # 2026-09-20 (autonomy loop #12): the 5-min agent-run reaper archives a
#                                           # SPAWNED child coding session PROPERLY (chat archivedAt + satellite, via
#                                           # archiveChat) once its plan board is complete, it holds no enabled
#                                           # schedule, has no live run and has not run for 6 h; the 7-day idle reap
#                                           # archives properly too. Metric child_session_archived {reason}. Set =1
#                                           # to leave finished sub-sessions at status ready (the pre-#12 clutter).
#                                           # (Also new: a finalize on the RETIRING colour un-parks the chat's hook
#                                           # rows for the new colour — metric finalize_handoff; no switch.)
#                                           # schedule inside the finalize through the sweep's own row pass
#                                           # (fireDueScheduleNow: same atomic claim, caps, delta gate, bookkeeping)
#                                           # instead of waiting for the next 30 s sweeper tick — 3 of 4 slots had
#                                           # gone to message wakes that found the idle chat first. A schedule that
