# ── Decision gate (2026-09-24, owner: "build it all … with TypeSafe's API, then the open-source alternative") ──
# The `decision` model seat (Account → Admin → Endpoints → Model roles) answers the harness's own small
# judgments with a Jev-class DECISION MODEL (typed noul / choice / score + calibrated probabilities, one
# prefill, zero output tokens) instead of a reasoning-model generation. Every gated site fails OPEN.
# PROD: set the GitHub secret TYPESAFE_API_KEY — deploy.yml writes it into the web-fleet .env and into box C's
# deploy-managed /opt/crossmodel-local/env-secrets.env (2026-09-25); docker-compose.app.yml forwards TYPESAFE_* to backend + worker.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=            # built-in "jev" backend: TypeSafe Jev (https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone). Set it here on
#                              # every box, OR register api.typesafe.ai/v1 as a "Decision model" endpoint in the admin UI
#                              # (key stored encrypted in the DB, reaches all boxes) and seat it on "Decision gate".
# TYPESAFE_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai/v1   # override the host (Vercel AI Gateway: https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/typesafe/v1)
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-1.13.0    # model id sent to the built-in jev backend. PINNED to the versioned id (E4, 2026-09-25): the
#                              # `jev-latest` alias moves on every vendor release and would silently invalidate every fitted
#                              # threshold / temperature. Every decision row records the id the server ANSWERED with
#                              # (meta.modelId) and a change under a fixed request id raises a throttled warn.
# DECISION_GATE_DEFAULT_MODE=shadow   # off | shadow | act — shadow records what the gate WOULD decide next to what the
#                                     # reasoning path did (loop_metrics decision_gate); act lets a purpose skip work
# ── Decision-gate SPEND rows (2026-09-28, owner: "did you make sure to add jev to api costs as well" — it had not been) ──
# Every ANSWERED decision call (the primary leg — whichever leg answered —, every challenger, the admin probe; never a
# memo hit) mints run_tokens_in (+ run_tokens_out when > 0) + ONE run_spend row with meta.profile='decision',
# meta.model = the backend's model id (jev-1.13.0 / cql-litellm:agx-laya / deepseek-flash), meta.purpose / backend /
# backendSpec / decisionId (meta.challenger on challenger rows), sessionId = the chat the decision served else the
# synthetic 'decision-gate' session — so Account → Admin → API costs (and GET /admin/model-roles/decision-registry
# calls24h / costUsd24h) count Jev. Prices: TypeSafe Jev = the VENDOR LIST price (docs.typesafe.ai/models: "$42 per
# billion input tokens" = $0.042 / M input, output not metered); a registry backend = the model entry's
# usdPerMTokIn/Out, else the endpoint's settings.usdPerMTokIn/Out, else $0 badged "self-hosted"; the DeepSeek readout
# = the coding cost table's deepseek-flash rate. History before this deploy: scripts/framework-audit/
# backfill-decision-gate-spend.js via prodq.sh (dry-run default, --apply, idempotent on meta.decisionId).
# TYPESAFE_USD_PER_MTOK_IN=0.042       # override the Jev INPUT price (USD per 1M tokens; a prepaid pack / gateway markup) — rows say priceSource 'env'
# TYPESAFE_USD_PER_MTOK_OUT=0          # override the Jev OUTPUT price (list: not metered)
# LIVE STATE (2026-09-26 02:05Z): the STORE-BACKED admin mode (Account → Admin → Endpoints → Model roles → Decision gate;
# DECISION_GATE_STORE_MODE_DISABLED below) WINS over every DECISION_GATE_MODE_* line here — the values below are the env
# FALLBACK, not what runs. In act in prod: wake_triage, sweep_triage, imessage_send, auto_route, drain_triage (owner-directed
# flips 00:20Z / 01:49Z / 02:05Z); every other purpose shadow. Docs: docs/DECISION_MODEL_ENHANCEMENTS_2026-09-25.md §6.1.
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_WAKE_TRIAGE=shadow      # hooks: park a non-alarm supervisor wake the gate is confident needs no turn now
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_DELTA_MATERIAL=shadow   # schedules: skip a delta-gate fire whose probe change is immaterial
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_AUTO_ROUTE=shadow       # mode='auto': L1/L2/L3 from the gate instead of the regex heuristic
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_IMESSAGE_SEND=shadow    # skip the 8 s send-intent utility call when the gate is confident it is not a send
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_BROWSER_DRIVER=shadow   # cloud / Mac / computer from the gate instead of a GLM reasoning call
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_MEMORY_EXTRACT=shadow   # skip memory extractors the gate is confident have nothing to extract
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_SELF_AUDIT=shadow       # skip the coding self-audit round when the gate is confident the final is evidenced
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_GUARD_STRIKE=shadow     # N1 (2026-09-25): the nightly strike adjudicator puts every strike it labelled tonight to the gate
#                                            # (Choice true_positive / false_positive / unclear) and records the pass's verdict as the label —
#                                            # the only purpose with a labelled corpus on day one; act = the gate adjudicates the ambiguous
#                                            # strikes past the 30/night reasoning cap (confident, never 'unclear'; labelled rows never re-written)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_SWEEP_TRIAGE=shadow     # N2 (2026-09-25): a stock fleet/project SWEEP firing is judged over a CODE-COMPUTED delta since the
#                                            # previous sweep (runs finished/failed, hook events, open asks, tickets, status card, last note);
#                                            # shadow = the stash rides the fired sweep and its finalize labels it (acted ⇒ needed the turn);
#                                            # act (designed, NOT enabled) = skip a confidently quiet sweep, bounded by the heartbeat floor below
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_CODING_MEMORY_FOLD=shadow  # N3 (2026-09-25): ONE prefill of per-leg nouls before the post-run coding-memory legs (session
#                                            # summary / project fold / user prefs — coding-memory.service) and the run-journal distillation
#                                            # (run-journal.service); shadow = each leg is judged next to whether its extractor actually CHANGED
#                                            # the stored doc (content diff; LLM/parse failure = unlabelled); act (designed, NOT enabled) = a
#                                            # leg the gate is confident has nothing to fold is skipped (no utility call, doc untouched)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_REFLECTION_ROUTE=shadow # N8 (2026-09-25): on a 3× tool streak a typed Choice {retry_with_corrected_params, different_tool,
#                                            # deterministic_framework, needs_diagnosis} over the packaged StreakEvidence, CONCURRENT with the
#                                            # 45 s Double-Checker consult (no latency added for a normal consult; a FAST consult — keyless seat /
#                                            # seat error — waits ≤ 250 ms for the gate, then labels async); shadow = judged next to the remedy the
#                                            # consult's advice prescribed (or the lane's next tool call); act (designed, NOT enabled) = a confident
#                                            # non-needs_diagnosis route skips the consult and a one-line typed hint rides the breaker notice
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_CLAIM_EVIDENCED=shadow  # N5 (2026-09-25): the action verifier mines deed-claim candidates DETERMINISTICALLY first (2026-09-26: tool-name
#                                            # receipt lines + receipt-anchored verbs in any person — the first-person miner alone never fired on real notes) and asks
#                                            # ONE noul per mined claim ("evidenced by this run's receipts") over the code-computed executed pool,
#                                            # CONCURRENTLY with the utility-LLM claim extraction (shadow adds zero latency); label = the verifier's
#                                            # own per-claim verdict (convicted / exonerated / unjudged). act (designed, NOT enabled) = await the gate
#                                            # in place of the LLM call and skip the extraction when EVERY mined claim is confidently evidenced —
#                                            # the tier chain still judges every claim; verdicts stay observe-only
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_DRAIN_TRIAGE=shadow     # N6 (2026-09-25): a queued AGENT-message batch about to drain as a detached turn is judged over a
#                                            # code-computed state (rows / senders / ages / question-or-request / sender-awaits-reply / failure cues /
#                                            # superseded markers / open directives / user rows waiting; bodies LAST ≤ 4k) — Choice ack_only / coalesce /
#                                            # act_now; shadow = the stash rides the drained run and its finalize labels it (acted ⇒ act_now);
#                                            # act (designed, NOT enabled) = park a confidently quiet batch for one defer window (never with a user row behind it)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_SUPERVISOR_TURN_NOOP=shadow  # agent-decisions 2026-09-27 (area supervisor): before a stock SWEEP firing (coding/schedule.service) or a
#                                            # queued AGENT-message drain (chat-agent drainChatQueue) ONE noul `will_act` is asked over the TARGET's own record —
#                                            # 7-day no-op / action rates, consecutive no-ops, minutes since the last action (loop_metrics supervisor_noop /
#                                            # _action / _note), its last three notes (kind + ≤160-char head), board counts (open directives, lanes running,
#                                            # pending hook events, owner asks, user rows waiting) — then the pending inputs LAST (≤8 rows, heads ≤300, source
#                                            # ids hashed; state ≤4k). `has_new_input` is a SHADOW PROBE labelled at decision time from the DETERMINISTIC
#                                            # trigram-containment rule (platform/supervisor-turn-noop.ts hasNewInput) — the rule itself is a HARD PIN in the
#                                            # act contract, never the model's answer. Hook wakes are NOT re-keyed: wake_triage can gain the same facts as an
#                                            # OPT-IN v3 `target_facts` block (DECISION_GATE_WAKE_TRIAGE_V3_ENABLED=1 below). A 'supervised chat' target
#                                            # (possibly a human's own conversation) ships note kind + age only — no reply heads leave the box. shadow = the
#                                            # stash rides the turn beside sweep_triage's / drain_triage's (asked CONCURRENTLY — facts 1.5 s + decide 4 s
#                                            # inside the sibling's budget, no serial latency; DecisionStash.also) and is labelled from what the turn did:
#                                            # a MUTATING PLATFORM TOOL CALL in the transcript ⇒ acted — the model's own "ACTIONS TAKEN" marker is a claim,
#                                            # not evidence (fixer 2026-09-27); the 7-day rates in the state are themselves regex-over-model-markers
#                                            # (loop_metrics rows the watchdog classifies), features never labels. A PINNED turn (new input / alarm / cap
#                                            # bypass / waiting user row — the rule can never skip it) stamps `pinned:true` on its row, which is
#                                            # excludeFromFit: the band holds only turns the rule could skip. act (designed, admitted by the readiness ruler
#                                            # only — 30 band rows at Wilson-LB ≥ 0.95 and, once act-period floor turns exist, 30 of them with a quiet-rate
#                                            # Wilson-LB ≥ 0.95 i.e. floor-turn action rate ≤ 5%; auto-demote bar 0.95) = a confidently quiet turn
#                                            # (will_act ≤ 1−τ, τ 0.85) with no pin is NOT started: a sweep firing is skipped (lastStatus
#                                            # 'skipped:turn_noop:<n>', cap token refunded), a drain batch is parked (Redis marker, re-drained after the
#                                            # defer window); both record wake_parked reason 'turn_noop'; the heartbeat floor runs the turn on every Nth
#                                            # tick regardless and marks its label `control:true` (the band's act-period labels). Once act it REPLACES
#                                            # sweep_triage and drain_triage at those sites (supervisorTurnNoopActive). Replay (AR0926 idiom, 2026-09-27):
#                                            # n=341, coverage 17%, band agreement 77.6% (LB 65.3%) vs the 58% schedule-origin no-op base rate ⇒ build-shadow.
# DECISION_GATE_SUPERVISOR_TURN_NOOP_HEARTBEAT_TICKS=3  # act-mode floor: a quiet turn still RUNS on every Nth eligible tick (clamped 2..24)
# DECISION_GATE_SUPERVISOR_TURN_NOOP_DEFER_MIN=15       # act-mode drain park length in minutes (clamped 5..60); a sweep skip waits for its own next tick
# DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_SUPERVISOR_TURN_NOOP=0.85     # acting confidence on `will_act` (noul ≤ 1−τ ⇒ quiet)
#                                            # wake_triage request. wake_triage is an ACT purpose, so flip this only after a v2-vs-v3 replay: when on, the
#                                            # request uses the v3 question set (own questionsHash ⇒ own readiness partition + memo key — a regression is
#                                            # measured, never pooled with the v2 act rows); the lookup runs CONCURRENTLY with the lane lookup under the
#                                            # one 1.5 s WAKE_TRIAGE_LANE_LOOKUP_MS budget (no serial wall clock added to a hook group)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_WAKE_EFFORT=shadow      # N9 (2026-09-25): every MACHINE wake (hook / schedule / agent drain / webhook) is scored 0–2 "how much
#                                            # deliberation does this wake need" over code flags + the wake HEAD (≤ 2 KB), CONCURRENTLY with the
#                                            # orchestrator call (no latency added); the finalize labels it from what the wake did (0 no-op / 1 note /
#                                            # 2 acted-or-escalated) with the run's length and cost. act (built, DOUBLE-LOCKED — see the owner switch
#                                            # below) = a non-alarm wake confidently scored ≤ 1 runs its built-in glm/deepseek seat at reasoning_effort
#                                            # 'high' instead of 'max'; alarm-class wakes ([run_failed] … / [INFRA ALERT]) are pinned to max regardless
# DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_<PURPOSE>=0.85     # per-purpose acting confidence (clamped to [0.5, 1]; callers carry defaults —
#                                            # guard_strike 0.9, sweep_triage 0.85, wake_triage 0.85, delta_material 0.85,
#                                            # coding_memory_fold 0.8, reflection_route 0.85, claim_evidenced 0.9 (HIGH side
#                                            # acts: noul ≥ τ), drain_triage 0.85; DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_DRAIN_TRIAGE_<OPTION> per option; firing_superseded 0.9, tool_intent 0.85,
#                                            # wake_effort 0.9)
# DECISION_GATE_CLAIM_EVIDENCE_MAX_CLAIMS=8  # N5: mined claims per request (1–20; by position, so questionsHash depends only on the count)
# DECISION_GATE_DRAIN_TRIAGE_DEFER_MIN=15    # N6 act-mode park length in minutes (clamped 5..60); a parked batch is never re-triaged — the orphan
#                                            # sweeper re-drains it after the park; USER rows never wait behind a park
#                                            # agreement 43 % — 20/46, 48 % act_now→ack_only over-acting — so a stored / env 'act' runs as
#                                            # SHADOW, source 'registry_cap', and the admin PUT refuses act). Unset = capped. Generic shape
#                                            # DECISION_GATE_<PURPOSE>_ACT_CAP_DISABLED for any purpose in decision-gate-modes PURPOSE_ACT_CAPS.
# DECISION_GATE_GUARD_STRIKE_NIGHTLY_CAP=200 # N1: gate calls per nightly pass (labelled strikes first, newest first; clamped 0..2000; 0 = none)
# DECISION_GATE_SWEEP_HEARTBEAT_TICKS=3      # N2 act-mode floor: a quiet sweep still FIRES on every Nth due tick (clamped 2..24), so a missed
#                                            # stuck lane waits at most (N−1) cadences; hook wakes never pass through the sweep gate
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_CHECKER_ROUTE=shadow      # N4 (2026-09-25): the Level 2 checker-site router — its OWN purpose (review: sharing auto_route let the
#                                              # router's flip-readiness stamp measure checker rows). Shadow = depth / needs_live_web asked beside the
#                                              # isSimpleQuestion regex, never awaited, labelled at the chat finalize. act = a confident simple_lookup
#                                              # takes the 75 s checker path + the Double Checker at reasoning_effort 'high'; a confident contestable
#                                              # forces the full wait; the checker is never skipped on the gate alone. Threshold
#                                              # DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_CHECKER_ROUTE (default 0.7).
# DECISION_GATE_CHECKER_ROUTE_DISABLED=1       # kill switch (N4): the Level 2 checker site never consults the gate — the regex alone picks the
#                                              # 75 s vs 300 s checker wait, exactly as before
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_ROUTE_LABEL_WINDOW_DISABLED=1  # kill switch (patience plan 1a): PICKED-level user sends stop firing the shadow auto_route
#                                                   # gate (actual = the level the user picked; note user_picked). Only modeSource='picked'
#                                                   # fires it (§4.2 — a default / restored / unsignalled level is not a human label), and only
#                                                   # once the send is admitted past the deep-research reserve. The web client sends
#                                                   # modeSource since 2026-09-26 (mobile does not yet).
# LABEL_WINDOW_SAMPLE_PERCENT=100              # patience plan 1a: share of picked-level signed-in sends the label window scores (0 = none)
# LABEL_WINDOW_DECISION_SPEC=seat              # patience plan 1a: the backend the label window asks. Default 'seat' = the decision seat's normal
#                                              # chain (TypeSafe Jev in prod) since 2026-09-26 — owner Q1 (TypeSafe egress for explicit-level sends)
#                                              # answered by asking for the back-test over all user chats; the web client sends modeSource since
#                                              # the same day. 'deepseek-flash' = the pre-Q1 logprob readout (a provider that already saw every
#                                              # chat message); any other registered spec pins that backend
# DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_AUTO_ROUTE_DEEP_RESEARCH=0.85  # per-option Level 3 acting bar for auto_route; the generic DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_
#                                                        # AUTO_ROUTE can never LOWER it below 0.85 (only this explicit env can — the Phase 2 refit)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_FIRING_SUPERSEDED=shadow # N7 (2026-09-25): a busy-parked MACHINE recurring firing (busySkips > 0) that claims a free lane is judged
#                                            # against the run that held the lane (its final ≤1.5k + code-counted receipts, minutes since, parked
#                                            # minutes, next cadence) — Choice fire / drop_superseded / merge_into_next. One-shots, owner-authored
#                                            # (promptSetBy user/NULL) and owner-subscribed rows are NEVER judged. shadow = the stash rides the
#                                            # fired run and its finalize labels it (real work ⇒ 'fire' was right); act (designed, NOT enabled) =
#                                            # a confident drop/merge skips the firing (lastStatus skipped:superseded | skipped:merged_next, cap
#                                            # token refunded, busySkips reset, next cadence unchanged). Metric schedule_parked_claim records every
#                                            # parked firing that starts (gate on or off); schedule_superseded_skip counts act skips.
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_TOOL_INTENT=shadow      # N10 (2026-09-25): SHADOW TELEMETRY ONLY (no act consumer exists): once per coding tool turn (its first
#                                            # dispatched call; a batched turn shares one narration — batch size in the row) the gate picks which
#                                            # listed tool the turn's own reasoning/content tails intended (positional option_1..n; option_1 = the
#                                            # emitted tool; tool results never enter the state) next to the regex detector; a one-option set is
#                                            # not asked. Two outcome rows per decision, meta.label 'regex' (the detector's verdict — the only
#                                            # label the fit reads) and 'next_call' (the next turn's first tool; the run's last turn has none).
#                                            # Fire-and-forget beside the tool execution — no loop latency.
# DECISION_GATE_TOOL_INTENT_DISABLED=1       # kill switch (N10): the agent loop never consults the gate for intent
# DECISION_GATE_TOOL_INTENT_RUN_CAP=16       # N10: gate calls (tool turns asked) per coding run (clamped 0..200; 0 = none)
# DECISION_GATE_WAKE_EFFORT_ACT_ENABLED=0    # N9 HARD DISABLE of the act path (0 / false / off): a calibrated act answer is recorded but NEVER lowers a
#                                            # wake's effort. Unset / 1 = allowed (owner lock LIFTED 2026-09-26 late — "default all chats to auto even
#                                            # supervisors": act flips through the store-backed mode + READY admission like every purpose; the
#                                            # 2026-09-22 "machine wakes keep max" directive is superseded). From 2026-09-25 to 09-26 this was the
#                                            # opt-IN owner switch (default OFF)
#                                            # label (2 = mutating tool OR the model's "ACTIONS TAKEN" marker). Unset = the HARNESS label:
#                                            # 2 ⇔ ≥ 3 evidence-bearing tool calls OR a mutating platform tool, 1 ⇔ 1–2 evidence calls, 0 ⇔ none;
#                                            # rows stamp meta.labelSource ('harness' | 'legacy'), meta.legacyLabel (the proxy, always) and
#                                            # meta.evidenceCalls; wake_triage / sweep_triage / drain_triage rows gain meta.harnessActed only.
# DECISION_GATE_TEMP=1.0                     # temperature for the logprob readout backends (DECISION_GATE_TEMP_<PURPOSE> per purpose);
#                                            # clamped to [0.7, 10] (WI-I 2026-09-25). FIT it from shadow rows, never guess:
#                                            #   cd backend && npm run decision-gate:fit -- --days=14 [--purpose=wake_triage]
#                                            # (NLL fit over meta.logits — the readout persists its raw per-option logprobs on
#                                            # every decision row — paired with the outcome's actual; prints the line below)
# DECISION_GATE_TEMP_WAKE_TRIAGE=            # per-purpose fitted temperature (the DeepSeek readout saturates at 0/1 at T=1, so
#                                            # the wake_triage threshold has no margin until this is fitted); stage on A, B AND C
# Flip readiness (E1, 2026-09-25 — docs/DECISION_MODEL_ENHANCEMENTS_2026-09-25.md §4 E1 / §6): the same script now prints,
# per (backend, purpose), the ONLY numbers that may justify an act flip — TypeSafe Jev rows paired via meta.answers (not just
# readout meta.logits), deduped by meta.stateHash, partitioned by meta.questionsHash: AUROC of (1 − confidence) as an error
# detector, coverage at ≤5% error, and precision inside the ACT BAND at the purpose's REAL cutoff (DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_
# <PURPOSE> or the consumer's default: noul ≤ 0.15 / 0.2, choice confidence ≥ 0.7 / 0.85 — never 0.5) → READY / NOT READY.
#   cd backend && npm run decision-gate:fit -- --days=14 --stamp     # --stamp writes instance:decision-gate/readiness
# Outcome rows now carry thresholdUsed / inActBand / agreedAtCutoff (+ per-option probabilities for a choice) so agreement is
# measurable at the cutoff. Admin readout: GET /admin/model-roles/decision-readiness (Model roles → Decision gate → Flip readiness).
# IN-PROCESS JOB (E1 job, 2026-09-25 — the CLI could not run in the prod image: no scripts/ dir, no tsx): the worker's durable
# cron `decision-gate-readiness` (platform/decision-gate-readiness.job.ts) now computes the SAME report over the last
# DECISION_GATE_READINESS_WINDOW_DAYS of decision_gate rows, stamps EVERY purpose (17) READY / NOT READY with reasons (the E12
# admission contract — an admin act flip is admitted the moment a purpose's bars hold, nobody runs a script), stores the full
# report under instance:decision-gate/readiness-report (what the admin GET returns + computedAt; the GET never recomputes), and
# records one loop_metrics row per purpose (kind decision_gate_readiness, meta {purpose, backend, ready, labels, spanDays, auroc,
# coverage5, bandN, bandPrecision, reasons}). Postgres-leased ⇒ ONE worker per firing (box A cron-only or box C), never the web
# boxes. Any failure writes NOTHING. The CLI moved to backend/src/scripts/ so dist/ carries it: inside the image run
#   node dist/scripts/decision-gate-fit-temperature.js --days=14 --stamp   (npm run decision-gate:fit picks dist when built, else tsx)
# DECISION_GATE_READINESS_JOB_DISABLED=1     # kill switch: the cron job never computes / stamps / stores / records (CLI unaffected)
# DECISION_GATE_READINESS_INTERVAL_MIN=360   # job cadence in minutes (clamped 15..10080; the worker registers it at boot)
# DECISION_GATE_READINESS_WINDOW_DAYS=14     # job report window in days (clamped 1..90) — the CLI's --days
#                                            # (readers fail CLOSED — no stamp = NOT READY; no purpose is ever flipped by this)
# ROLLOUT SELF-GOVERNANCE (2026-09-27 — docs/DECISION_GATE_ROLLOUT_PLAYBOOK.md): the act flips are the FRAMEWORK's job now. The
# decision-role REGISTRY (platform/decision-gate-registry.ts — every purpose's tier, consumer, what act does, label, bars, caps,
# kill switches; GET /admin/model-roles/decision-registry; the get_decision_gate_status tool) is the source of truth, and the
# worker cron `decision-gate-rollout` (platform/decision-gate-rollout.ts; runs every DECISION_GATE_ROLLOUT_INTERVAL_MIN but judges
# each readiness report ONCE, so effectively once per readiness firing) flips every TIER-1 purpose in shadow whose READY stamp is
# fresh AND MEASURED (a real backend, labels ≥ the bar — never an owner-override stamp) and not act-capped to act THROUGH THE ADMIN
# PUT's OWN ADMISSION (updateDecisionModes: caps, stamp, primary pin, control gate), records one loop_metrics decision_gate_rollout
# row per action, parks a purpose auto-demoted twice in 7 d for 7 d, files ONE owner question per ready tier-2/3 purpose (deduped
# while open; a tier-2 'flip' answer flips on the next pass), never touches an OFF purpose, and REPORTS (never rewrites) a store
# row that says act for a code-capped purpose. The owner briefing, the framework-facts prompt layer (shadow / off / parked /
# capped lists, the tier rule, recent actions) and the Fleet Supervisor's get_decision_gate_status / set_decision_gate_mode
# tools read the same ledger (store row instance:decision-gate/rollout).
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_ROLLOUT=0               # env BOOT DEFAULT of SystemSetting decision_gate_auto_rollout (default ON — the owner's
#                                            # 2026-09-25 pre-authorisation); the row wins: PUT /admin/model-roles/decision-rollout
#                                            # { enabled } or Account → Admin → Endpoints → Model roles → Decision gate → registry panel
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_ROLLOUT_DRY_RUN=1       # the automaton records + logs what it WOULD flip (loop_metrics rows carry dryRun:true) and writes no mode
# DECISION_GATE_ROLLOUT_JOB_DISABLED=1       # kill switch: the cron computes nothing (the admin PUT / the tools still flip by hand)
# DECISION_GATE_LIFECYCLE_ENFORCE_DISABLED=1 # (2026-10-20 DECISION-GATE-LIFECYCLE) the automaton no longer sets a SHADOW purpose off when it is past its
#                                            # registry reviewBy with the reviewBar unmet, or reads AUROC < 0.6 on >= 200 labels over >= 10 d
#                                            # (non-converging — one re-pose ticket); decision_gate_lifecycle_retired rows stop
# DECISION_GATE_ROLLOUT_INTERVAL_MIN=60      # cadence in minutes (clamped 15..10080); a pass on an already-judged readiness report is a no-op
#                                            # (Account → Admin → Endpoints → Model roles → Decision gate; one row, every box within
#                                            # 30 s) and run env-only modes on this process. Unset = the stored mode wins over env.
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_COMPUTE_POLICY=shadow   # compute policy (2026-09-26): D0 at send, concurrent with the lead's step 0 — `depth` choice
#                                            # {simple_lookup, ordinary, contestable, unclear} + `stakes` / `needs_live_web` / `research_request`
#                                            # nouls over message ≤4k + last two user turns ≤1k + attachment count + this chat's prior
#                                            # rung/escalations, ≤1200 ms. act = a confident simple_lookup ∧ ¬stakes SKIPS the checker; stakes ∧
#                                            # contestable waits ≤ STAKES_WAIT_MS at lead effort max; research_request (signed-in + quota) starts a
#                                            # background council. shadow = the preset plan + the row. Labels: escalated (Dig deeper tap ≤30 min,
#                                            # PRIMARY), reask_5m, thumbs+reason, revision_material outcome, checker_skipped_material
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_DRAFTS_AGREE=shadow     # D1 when the first answer is ready: one noul over lead final ≤3k + checker draft ≤3k. act = agree ≥0.8
#                                            # skips the reconcile pass (pill 'checked'); shadow = the reconcile runs as today and its
#                                            # revision_material verdict is the label
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_REVISION_MATERIAL=shadow # D1b when a reconcile lands: DECIDES only when the deterministic numbers / times / dates / entities /
#                                            # negations diff says unchanged. act = wording-only ⇒ 'checked' with no rewrite; fallback = material
#                                            # (today's rewrite). In shadow a diff-decided reconcile ALSO asks the gate for the row (audit
#                                            # gate-runtime-4, 2026-09-26: the diff fired on every real reconcile ⇒ zero rows). Label: user
#                                            # thumbs / escalation after the revision
#                                            # "10:00"→"10 am", "$1,200"→"$1 200" and sentence-initial capitals all read as material changes)
#                                            # revision_material row only when the diff said unchanged — i.e. never in practice)
# DECISION_GATE_MODE_TASK_KIND=shadow        # task-aware pick (2026-10-20): the job type of a human turn, asked beside turn_plan (platform/task-kind.ts).
#                                            # ACT-CAPPED in code (a pure evidence key — a stored / env 'act' runs shadow, the PUT refuses it);
#                                            # off = no ask. Whether the kind-aware pick LEADS is the modelPickKind store mode, never this mode
# DECISION_GATE_DISABLED=1                   # kill switch: no gate makes any call (probe included)
# Calibrated-only acting + per-leg budgets + readout censoring (E2, 2026-09-25): decide() returns
# `calibrated` (true for a systemone backend, or a logprob readout whose purpose has a FITTED
# DECISION_GATE_TEMP_<PURPOSE>); an act purpose answered by an UNCALIBRATED backend comes back as
# mode 'shadow' (row meta.modeDowngrade='uncalibrated', requestedMode='act') so no consumer acts on
# a 0/1 readout after a Jev failure — consumers key their act branch on the RESULT's mode.
# Auth latch + backend-down alert (audit budgets-cost-6, 2026-09-26): a decision backend that answers HTTP 401/403 (revoked
# / exhausted key — prod saw a 5-min TypeSafe 403 episode on 2026-09-26 06:34Z) is LATCHED: the leg loop skips it for the
# cooldown with an attributable legErrors entry ('TypeSafe Jev: latched (HTTP 403 at …; re-probe at …)'), ONE ask per
# cooldown carries the half-open probe (success clears it, another 401/403 re-latches, any other error releases it —
# fail-open), a `spec`-pinned ask (the admin Test button) always calls. The first latch of an episode writes ONE
# loop_metrics row kind decision_gate_backend_down {event:'latched'} ('relatched' / 'recovered' follow) and raises an
# [INFRA ALERT — decision backend down] wake through fleet/infra-watch (deduped 6 h per backend + status; the infra sweep
# re-reads the rows under the same key); an ask that loses EVERY leg writes {event:'all_legs_failed'} and alerts on a
# streak (3 in 5 min). decide() now returns `downgraded:true` next to mode 'shadow' when an act purpose was answered by an
# uncalibrated backend; the readiness stamp carries per-purpose `health` {calls, fails, downgraded, fellThrough, latched}
# and get_fleet_telemetry view 'boxes' carries a `decisionGate` tile. The 429/529 retry and the fail-open contract are unchanged.
# DECISION_GATE_AUTH_LATCH_MS=90000          # cooldown per latch (clamped 10000..600000); one probe ask per cooldown
#                                              # sweep (the decision_gate_backend_down rows and the 'boxes' tile stay; the latch itself is unaffected)
#                                            # page shows "latch view disabled here" instead of the answering process's 401/403 latch state (the latch itself,
#                                            # the stamp's per-purpose `health` counters and the fleet tile are untouched; the map is per PROCESS — the worker keeps its own)
# Per-purpose backends + challengers + open-weight systemone servers (2026-09-26, owner: "support the open weight version
# of jev for testing different decision models … we are self hosting laya now"). Every candidate — TypeSafe Jev, Laya
# (`laya-serve`, :8000), JevK5 (`jevk5-serve`, :8090), NeoHorse-Jev (`neohorse-decision serve`, :8080), openjev (vLLM;
# CC BY-NC — testing only) — speaks POST /v1/systemone and is registered as a "Decision model (/systemone)" endpoint; the
# admin panel Model roles → Decision gate → "Decision backends per purpose" (GET/PUT /admin/model-roles/decision-backends,
# store row instance:decision-gate/backends, every box within 30 s) sets per purpose a PRIMARY (first chain leg) and
# CHALLENGERS (asked in parallel, shadow rows only — never answer, never act, never feed auto-demote). Rows carry
# meta.backendSpec; the readiness job groups by it and stamps each purpose on its CONFIGURED primary, so a primary change
# on an act purpose drops that purpose to shadow until the job re-stamps the new backend (≤ 6 h). Fail-open throughout:
# a bad / missing backends row = the seat chain; challengers can only add telemetry.
#                                            # again — 'machine' / 'supervisor' decision_gate rows (meta.segment, stamped by decide() opts.segment on the
#                                            # decision / challenger / outcome rows) re-enter the human sample and the backend's call counts; default: they
#                                            # form their own (backend, purpose, segment) groups that are never the stamp and never READY
# DECISION_GATE_CHALLENGER_MAX=2             # challengers asked per decision (the purpose's list, else the default list, minus the leg that answered)
# DECISION_GATE_CHALLENGER_GRACE_MS=0        # an OPTIONAL wait after the primary answers (default 0 since the 2026-09-26 Laya follow-up — challengers are
#                                            # DETACHED and add no latency; ceiling 10 s; the legacy default 400 applies under the detach kill switch)
# DECISION_GATE_CHALLENGER_TIMEOUT_MS=5000   # a detached challenger's OWN deadline from t0 (clamped 500..60000, independent of the caller's deadline —
#                                            # Laya's proxy serialises requests, up to ~2 s under load); on expiry its row reads ok:false 'challenger_timeout'
#                                            # every still-running challenger as a timeout at once; nothing outlives the caller's deadline
# Laya via LiteLLM (2026-09-26 follow-up; llm.cql.ca `agx-laya`, live-probed): the proxy serves typed decisions through POST /chat/completions
# with a `questions` map and a JSON answers envelope in the message content (`/v1/systemone` 404s; a logprobs chat call 400s). Prod already
# registers the proxy as the `cql-litellm` openai_chat endpoint with all 37 models, so the transport is a PER-MODEL flag: tick [typed decisions]
# (`decision: 'systemone_chat'`) on `agx-laya` in the Endpoints dialog + max state chars ≈ 3800 (the proxy silently cuts the state at 1,024 input
# tokens); the gate then calls it with the systemone_chat transport (row backendKind 'systemone', label "<label> (typed decisions via chat
# completions)"). A proxy that serves ONLY decision models may instead be registered with providerShape 'systemone_chat'.
#                                                # choice's confidence = probabilities[choice], a score's = the max level probability (Laya reports
#                                                # 1 − normalised entropy — a different scale from Jev's); the server value rides meta.confidenceRaw
# Laya failure telemetry (2026-09-26 audit gate-runtime-5): the Python-serialised chat envelope carries NaN / Infinity VALUES on a question the
# model could not score (checker_route's `needs_live_web`, 14/14 prod rows — beside a VALID `depth`), and an HTTP 400's body was dropped from
# the row. Now: non-finite values are sanitised to null and the ONE unparsable question is censored (row meta.censoredAnswers {key: reason} +
# meta.nonFiniteTokens; the valid answers ship); an unparsable envelope names the token + index + window (or the parser error + head + tail);
# leg / challenger errors carry a scrubbed ≤ 300-char HTTP ≥ 400 body head (`… body: {…}`; Bearer / sk- redacted; row error cap 520).
# Sampled STATE corpus (ON BY DEFAULT since 2026-09-28 — backlog CT-9; it had been opt-in at 0 and prod held 0 rows all-time, so nothing could
# calibrate a non-Jev backend): a drawn ask writes ONE loop_metrics row kind 'decision_gate_state' { id, purpose, questionsHash, stateChars,
# state (capped), questions, backendSpec }; never on memo hits or probes; rows only — no model call, no spend. Export the laya-evals JSONL with
# `npm run decision-gate:export -- --purpose=wake_triage --days=28` (inside the image: node dist/scripts/decision-gate-export.js …).
# docker-compose.app.yml forwards RATE / RATE_WAKE_TRIAGE / DISABLED (+ the TEMP_AUTOFIT pair) to both services since 2026-09-28 — compose passes
# only LISTED vars, so a switch set in .env alone never reached the containers before.
# DECISION_GATE_STATE_SAMPLE_RATE=0.05       # global sampling rate 0..1 (built-in default 0.05; 0 = off; NODE_ENV=test defaults to 0)
# DECISION_GATE_STATE_SAMPLE_RATE_WAKE_TRIAGE=0.2  # per-purpose rate (…_<PURPOSE>, upper-cased) — wins over the global one (built-in per-purpose default: wake_triage 0.2)
# DECISION_GATE_STATE_SAMPLE_MAX_CHARS=12000 # the stored state text is cut here (clamped 500..200000; the row says stateSampleTruncated)
# DECISION_GATE_STATE_SAMPLE_DISABLED=1      # hard switch: no state row is ever written, whatever the rates say
# DECISION_GATE_STATE_RETENTION_DAYS=28      # the readiness cron deletes 'decision_gate_state' rows older than this (clamped 1..365; one indexed deleteMany)
# ── Decision-gate LABELS + READINESS (backlog group decision-gate, 2026-09-28: DOI-21 / E09 / E10 / E11 / E12 / E13 / E14 / CT-9) ──
# Every piece is shadow-safe and restores the previous behaviour on its own switch.
#                                            # harness-proxy row: pill updated / ≥ 3 lead tool calls ⇒ contestable, 1–2 ⇒ ordinary, none + short ⇒ simple_lookup)
# COMPUTE_POLICY_MACHINE_LABEL_MIN_ROWS=30   # DOI-21 ramp: `machine` rows are excludeFromFit until this many exist fleet-wide (clamped 0..10000; 0 = enter at once)
#                                            # source diff ⇒ material, fallback ⇒ wording-only, gate ⇒ acted + excluded); the human 'human' rows stay primary
#                                                     # (the pre-change guard — under it a parked stock sweep was never judged: 0 rows all-time)
#                                                     # clamp(10 × labels/day, 50, 200) floor, no precision-only waiver for a < 5 % minority class)
# DECISION_GATE_SWEEP_TRIAGE_CONTROL_RATE=0.1         # E12: share of confident-quiet ACT skips that FIRE as a control instead (0..1; default 1/10) — the stash
#                                                     # carries extra.control:true so the act band / auto-demote / the ruler's control rows measure the skip band
# SWEEP_TRIAGE_CONTROL_SAMPLE_DISABLED=1              # E12 kill switch: every confident-quiet act sweep is skipped again (the heartbeat floor alone fires)
# DECISION_GATE_WAKE_TRIAGE_CONTROL_RATE=0.1          # 2026-10-04: share of confident-quiet ACT wake_triage PARKS that DELIVER as a control instead
#                                                     # (0..1; default 1/10; blank / garbage = default) — a parked wake is never labelled, so without
#                                                     # this the act band held zero act-period labels; the control's stash carries extra.control:true
#                                                     # and its finalize label (mode act, in band, acted false) feeds the E12 + durable auto-demote
# WAKE_TRIAGE_CONTROL_SAMPLE_DISABLED=1               # kill switch: every confident-quiet act wake parks again (no control draw)
# DECISION_GATE_TOOL_INTENT_RETIRE_LIFTED=1           # E13: lifts tool_intent's registry RETIREMENT on this process (bare default mode 'shadow' again; the act cap
#                                                     # keeps its own lift env DECISION_GATE_TOOL_INTENT_ACT_CAP_DISABLED)
# DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_CODING_MEMORY_FOLD=0.8      # E14: restores the old act cutoff at the site AND in the ruler (the default moved to 0.9 on 2026-09-28)
# Offline cascade ruler (NO act-path cascade exists): `npm run decision-gate:cascade -- --days=14 --purpose=wake_triage --first='cql-litellm:agx-laya'
# --margin=0.03` pairs primary ↔ challenger ↔ outcome rows and prints, per τ 0.50–0.99, coverage / in-band precision / Δ vs the primary / the
# Learn-then-Test exact-binomial pass (α 0.10 δ 0.05, fixed-sequence strict→loose) — the act path is the next step after ≥ 1 week of paired rows.
# Systemone adapter tolerance + per-(backend, purpose) calibration (plan item A, integrated 2026-09-26 with the panel above —
# platform/decision-gate.ts): Laya's `distribution` score lists / array probabilities / noul-as-probabilities / missing `model`
# all parse; REGISTRY systemone bodies get stock noul criteria; a registry model's [max state chars] cuts the state per backend.
# "Calibrated" (what lets an act purpose ACT on an answer) is the built-in jev, a registered model the admin flagged
# [calibrated], or any backend with a FITTED temperature for (spec, purpose) — never a bare systemone server.
#                                                   # REGISTRY systemone servers (Laya requires the keys; TypeSafe / NeoHorse accept them)
# DECISION_GATE_TEMP_AUTOFIT_ENABLED=1       # OPT-IN (default OFF): the 6 h readiness job WRITES its READY temperature fits per (backend, purpose)
#                                            # into the backends row (`temps['<spec>|<purpose>']`, built-in jev excluded) — after which the runtime
#                                            # treats those pairs as CALIBRATED (an act purpose then acts on them). Unset = the fits are reported
#                                            # on the readiness page, never stored; a readout stays uncalibrated until DECISION_GATE_TEMP_<PURPOSE> is staged
# DECISION_GATE_TEMP_AUTOFIT_DISABLED=1      # hard kill switch: never write `temps`, whatever the opt-in says
# Endpoint model flags for decision servers (Endpoints dialog): [calibrated] = the admin asserts the server's probabilities are
# calibrated (an act purpose may act on them without a fitted temperature — never for Laya, which ships over-confident);
# "max state chars" = the gate truncates the state for that model (Laya's 512-token context ≈ 1,200; JevK5 / openjev / NeoHorse 16k tokens).
# DECISION_GATE_LEG_TIMEOUT_MS=2000          # per-leg cap (owner 2026-09-28: 1000 → 2000 after ~50 Jev 1 s timeouts/day) for every leg but the LAST (min(remaining, this)) so the fallback
#                                            # stays reachable inside the 1.5–2.5 s request-path budgets; 0 = whole deadline per leg (pre-E2)
#                                            # again instead of the censor floor (the 20th-ranked logprob, or lowest−1 nat) —
#                                            # the omission is why 707/707 prod readout nouls read exactly 0 or 1 (row meta.censored names the floored keys)
# Event-loop stall vs egress (ticket 4d476b9a, 2026-10-21): prod saw bursts of all_legs_failed asks where Jev AND the
# readout timed out in the same instant while live probes right after answered — the readout started 250–350 ms after
# Jev's timer was due, i.e. THIS process's event loop was blocked (a late timer also fires before the poll phase reads a
# reply already in the socket). decide() now times every failed leg against its own deadline (lateMs), the loop's busy
# share (performance.eventLoopUtilization) and a dispatch probe (a setImmediate after EVERY post a leg issues: lateness
# before the wire timer was armed is subtracted — wireLateMs) — decision-gate-stall.ts. A CONFIRMED stall = the meter
# saturated, or wireLateMs ≥ max(200 ms, 25 % of the leg's budget); the cheap signal = a timeout ≥ 50 ms late (wire-late
# when measured) or inside a window the loop was ≥ 80 % busy (≥ 200 ms active). Such a timeout may re-ask that SAME leg
# ONCE per ask: with the whole residual when no later leg can be called or what is left is under every later leg's
# minimum (the incident's own 1200 ms asks — the cheap signal is enough there); while a later leg could still answer in
# what is left, only on a CONFIRMED stall, bounded so each later leg keeps its reserve (the readout 1100 ms, Jev 400 ms)
# plus the lateness already seen, at most half of what is left and at most its own budget — so an on-time or merely late
# timeout leaves that later leg exactly its pre-ticket budget; never a retry under the retried leg's own minimum (Jev
# 120 ms, the readout 500 ms). A confirmed-stall retry still costs the later leg everything above its reserve. HTTP
# errors, refused connections and free-loop timeouts are never retried. The decision row carries meta.stall
# {retried, recovered, legs[]}; an all-failed ask's decision_gate_backend_down row carries cause stall | egress | provider
# | mixed | budget + legTimings + loopBusy. Cause 'stall' needs CONFIRMED evidence on every timeout; such a row keeps its
# row but never advances the streak alert nor the infra sweep count (the sweep re-checks the evidence on the row). A
# merely late timer (a hung backend) reads egress / mixed and alerts as before. The readiness health counters count a
# failed stall retry with its first attempt (one call per leg per ask; the switch below, set in the reading process,
# counts every entry as before). Leg budgets are unchanged (Jev's 595–1499 ms shares are 3.6–9× its 164 ms p50 — the
# timeouts were not a budget problem; the readout's half share stays as firing 42 set it).
# DECISION_GATE_STALL_RECOVERY_DISABLED=1    # restores the pre-change leg loop, rows and streak byte for byte (no attribution, no stall retry, stall rows alert again)
# Memo of identical asks (E3, 2026-09-25): sha256(purpose|questions|state), in-process LRU (500 entries), TTL below;
# a hit records its own decision row (meta.cached=true, cachedFrom=<original id>) and makes no backend call. Every
# decision AND outcome row carries meta.stateHash / meta.questionsHash (dedupe + question-rewrite partition keys).
# DECISION_GATE_MEMO_TTL_MS=600000           # memo TTL (default 10 min)
# E3b (2026-09-25, live defect: 0 cached rows / 37 min): the memo key is a MEMO-STABLE projection of the state, not the
# exact state — the wake_triage request carried whole-minute event ages + the batch count, so the busy re-ask of the
# same batch hashed differently every minute. A consumer passes decide() opts.memoState (wake_triage: bucketed ages +
# the batch's sorted event IDS; a new id = a fresh ask; memo:false for alarm rows / rows without ids); every other
# purpose gets the generic projection (numeric *_min / *_minutes / *_ago / age fields bucketed 0-5 / 5-15 / 15-60 /
# 60+ min, *_at / *At / timestamp / *_ts keys dropped). Rows carry BOTH meta.stateHash (exact state — the ruler's
# dedupe key) and meta.memoHash (the memo key). Only ok answers are memoised, as before.
# Flip admission + auto-demotion (E12, 2026-09-25): PUT /admin/model-roles/decision-modes refuses `act` (409, names the
# missing bar) unless the store key instance:decision-gate/readiness carries { <purpose>: { ready: true, at, metrics } }
# from the flip-readiness report (npm run decision-gate:fit), younger than the max age; a rolling window (last 100
# LABELLED outcomes inside the purpose's act band, on the purpose's ACT question, ≥ MIN_N of them) whose precision is
# CONFIDENTLY below the bar writes the purpose back to shadow in the store row and records a `decision_gate_demoted`
# telemetry row (outcome demoted|observed; meta nAct / lowerBound / upperBound / margin / windowSince / windowScope).
# ACT-PERIOD ONLY (fix 2026-09-26 — incident 00:24:40Z: wake_triage flipped to act at 00:20:54Z was demoted 4 min later on
# 47 SHADOW-era labels at 0.894 vs 0.9): the window admits only labels whose DECISION was made in act mode and is cleared
# whenever the purpose's effective mode moves (a flip starts the count at zero). The rule is a confidence bound, not a
# point estimate:   demote iff n_act ≥ MIN_N AND wilsonUpper95(k, n_act) < bar − margin
# (the 95% Wilson interval of the act-period precision lies wholly below the bar — a one-sided 97.5% test). The UPPER
# bound, not the lower: "LB < bar − 0.05" would demote 29/30 (one miss; LB 0.833) — a purpose at exactly the 0.9 bar 96%
# of the time at its first 30 act labels. Boundaries at bar 0.9 / margin 0: n=30 demotes at ≤ 23/30 (UB 0.882), n=47 at
# ≤ 38/47 (0.896), n=100 at ≤ 84/100 (0.899); the incident's 42/47 (UB 0.954) does NOT demote — 0.894 vs 0.9 is the
# readiness report's call (≥ 200 labels), not a 47-label window's. False demotion at a true 0.9 ≈ 3–4% per check; a true
# 0.8 is caught with 62% at n=47 / 87% at n=100.
# DECISION_GATE_ADMISSION_DISABLED=1         # kill switch: the PUT admits act without a readiness stamp (pre-E12)
# DECISION_GATE_READINESS_MAX_AGE_DAYS=7     # a READY stamp older than this is stale — re-run the report
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_DEMOTE_MIN_N=30         # ACT-PERIOD labelled act-band outcomes needed in the window before a breach can fire (5–100)
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_DEMOTE_MIN_PRECISION=0.9  # the act-band precision bar (the flip bar); the Wilson UPPER bound must fall under it
#                                              # READINESS mirror (R&D exp #6, 2026-09-26): a purpose is stamped READY only when the
#                                              # act-band precision Wilson 95% LOWER bound ≥ bar (burden of proof on the GRANT)
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_DEMOTE_MIN_PRECISION_WAKE_TRIAGE=0.9  # per-purpose bar override (…_<PURPOSE>, upper-cased purpose key); wins over the global
# DECISION_GATE_AUTO_DEMOTE_MARGIN=0         # extra tolerance BELOW the bar before the net pulls a purpose (0 ≤ m < 0.5; 0.05 = "confidently below 0.85").
#                                            # No counterweight is needed with the upper-bound test, hence 0 — raise it only to make the net MORE lenient.
# Outcome labels (WI-C, 2026-09-25): wake_triage / delta_material / self_audit shadow rows carry a HARNESS-derived
# `actual` (did the woken run act? did the fired run do real work? did the audit reopen a step?) recorded when the
# run they gated FINALIZES (the stash rides fireScheduleTarget → RunInput.decision / ChatAgentRunArgs.decision), so
# `agreed` is computable and a purpose can ever meet the flip bar. Labels only — no wake, firing or audit changes.
#                                            # also turns off the E5 honest labels below (memory_extract / imessage_send modal)
# Honest labels + cost stamps (E5, 2026-09-25 — docs/DECISION_MODEL_ENHANCEMENTS_2026-09-25.md §4): every one is
# telemetry only, shadow-safe, and fails open; each has its own switch.
#                                            # extractor's measured outcome (changed ⇒ true, noop ⇒ false, failure ⇒ null)
#                                            # confirm card's Send / Cancel no longer labels the decision (no Redis park)
#                                            # (adds the readout's ~0.8 s back to every browser task selection)
# DECISION_GATE_WAKE_TRIAGE_DEFER_MIN=30     # act-mode triage park length; clamped 5–105 (WI-R: must stay under the 2 h stale-quiet bound)
# Request redesigns (E7 / E8, 2026-09-25 — docs/DECISION_MODEL_ENHANCEMENTS_2026-09-25.md §4): SHADOW-only instrumentation; the
# act contracts are unchanged (wake_triage still parks on needs_turn_now alone; self_audit's v2 act condition is STRICTER than v1).
# Every decision row now carries meta.questionsHash so the fit report partitions rows by request shape (old vs new never pooled).
#                                            # fan-out (needs_turn_now + disposition choice {ack,coalesce,act_now,escalate_owner} + addressed_to_supervisor +
#                                            # contains_failure_or_block + urgency score) over code-computed state (event-kind histogram, question/failure/
#                                            # guard-replaced/owner-facing flags, source-lane status + last run, prose LAST ≤ 4000 chars)
# DECISION_GATE_THRESHOLD_WAKE_TRIAGE_<OPTION>=0.9   # per-option threshold for the wake_triage disposition choice (ACK / COALESCE / ACT_NOW / ESCALATE_OWNER);
#                                            # today only the shadow "v2 park:…" / "v2 deliver:…" readout in the outcome note reads it (nothing acts on it)
#                                            # receipts with scrubbed args/result heads + claims_unbacked / steps_unbacked + one step_<k>_evidenced noul per
#                                            # reviewed completed step (by position, so questionsHash depends only on the reviewed count)
# DECISION_GATE_SELF_AUDIT_STEP_NOULS=12     # per-step nouls per self_audit request (0–40; 0 = holistic + split only) — bounds the logprob-readout leg,
#                                            # which runs one prefill PER question (TypeSafe Jev answers the whole fan-out in one call)
# SESSION_SCOPE_MIN_RETENTION_HOURS=24    # rows younger than this are never evicted by the per-source session cap
# SESSION_SCOPE_HARD_CAP=6000             # scope-wide ceiling on session-scope rows (oldest-first)
# SANDBOX_EGRESS_GUARD_DISABLED=1         # host-level: removes the DIGBY-SANDBOX-* iptables chains (coding sandboxes regain VPC/IMDS reach — do not)
# MEM_HIT_KEEP_DAYS=7                    # a row hit within this window sorts ahead of never-hit rows in the session source cap

# ── Wake cadence (2026-09-27 tt-rd audit, sup/wake-cadence; default ON — set "1" to revert each) ──
# Diagnosis: a 30-min schedule fired into 50–250-min runs for eight days — 1,357 busy-skips, then (after the
# 2026-09-24 steer) every firing was delivered INTO the running run with the full prompt, so runs never ended
# (117…257 min, ~115k prompt tokens re-sent per turn, $566 of a $582 lane); nothing compared a cadence to the
# lane's run length; the project supervisor cut its own stock sweep to 30 min and the heal never restored it.
# SCHEDULE_ADAPTIVE_CADENCE_OWNER_ROWS=1  # ALSO stretch owner-authored rows (promptSetBy user / NULL) — default OFF: an owner-set cadence is never silently overridden
# SCHEDULE_ADAPTIVE_CADENCE_MAX_SEC=21600 # ceiling of the automatic stretch (default 6 h; clamped ≥ 1 h)
# PROJECT_SWEEP_FLOOR_HEAL_OWNER_ROWS=1   # the ensure heal ALSO restores a stock sweep whose interval the OWNER lowered — default OFF (fixer 2026-09-27: an owner-set cadence is never silently overridden; attribution = the newest schedule.update Activity row with an owner-interval / machine attribution source — INTERVAL_ATTRIBUTION_MACHINE_SOURCES — written by updateScheduleForUser)
# SUPERVISOR_REPORT_UP_IS_ACTION=1        # a project-supervisor wake whose only receipt is a send to the Fleet Supervisor counts as supervisor_action again (default: supervisor_report_up) AND the decision-outcome labels (wake_triage / sweep_triage / drain_triage / supervisor_turn_noop) label such a wake as acted again (fixer 2026-09-27)
# BLOCK_STREAK_BACKOFF_DISABLED=1         # revert the open-ended block-streak backoff (todo 27c215d6): after 3 consecutive near-identical blocked-no-end-date firing answers a recurring lane monitor doubles its cadence (ceiling 24 h) instead of re-reporting the same blocker; never pauses the row
# BLOCK_STREAK_CARDS_ENABLED=1                    # ALSO file the escalate-once owner question for a stuck monitor (default OFF, observe-first — the STOPPED_SCHEDULE_CARDS pattern)

# ── Computer-use harness (cu-diag fixes #2–#5, 2026-09-25; default ON — set "1" to revert) ──
# Diagnosis: the 2026-09-25 computer_task incident (fa6eb1b1 / f19b0636) — input landed (frontmost
# Terminal→TextEdit on byte-identical frames: the app opened on an uncaptured display) while the loop
# scored dead-input strikes, refused repeated screenshots as "degeneration", graded readable dark
# Terminal frames as degenerate (bytes/pixel), and accepted leaked DSML markup as the final answer.
#                                          # back to the legacy abort at 3 strikes. (macOS full-input sessions only.)
#                                          # an INCONCLUSIVE probe (keystroke refused / no frame / driver threw) is
#                                          # retried once, on the next genuine strike (strike 3, right before the
#                                          # legacy abort). Either way the probe fires only on the action that scored
#                                          # a strike — never on screenshots, waits or no-op keys.
# COMPUTER_CLICK_STRIKES_LEGACY=1          # fix #2: a no-op CLICK scores a dead-input strike again (default: advisory only,
#                                          # like no-op keys; type / modifier keys / scroll still strike).
# COMPUTER_DEGENERATION_GUARD_LEGACY=1     # fix #3: legacy repeated-action signature (screenshot refused on its 3rd call,
#                                          # cmd+space == space) and the nudge consumes a step again.
#                                          # is not offered to the vision model.
#                                          # read as "degenerate" again and the byte-identity watchdog disarms on them).
#                                          # Default: decoded 256-px thumbnail metric (jpeg-js: luma σ + colours + edges).
#                                          # even when it is leaked tool markup (DSML / <tool_result>); default = one
#                                          # corrective re-call, then a harness message instead of the leak.
#                                          # frontmost A→B / display M of K" line on each action result.

# ── Layered prompts (2026-09-27; AGENTS.md "2026-09-27 layered prompts") ──────
