# ── Cohesive chat — task-lifecycle doctrine + hand-back lint (2026-09-28, chat-agent/handback-detector.ts) ──
# HANDBACK_LINT_DISABLED=1                 # the finalize LINT records no loop_metrics `handback_detected` row (a HUMAN-turn final that
#                                          # ends by handing the asked work back — "say the word", "confirm the card", "shall I continue" —
#                                          # while work evidently remains: the loop's real step count reached maxSteps, or a WORK
#                                          # tool's staged confirmation envelope sits in the parts — an external-effect tool's card
#                                          # (share link, cross-chat message, autonomy grant) is the doctrine's third lifecycle state,
#                                          # not a hand-back, and a deadline collapse alone never fires an offer-shaped closing).
#                                          # Observe-only either way: the lint never rewrites or blocks an answer; the doctrine (rule
#                                          # task.lifecycle, core + chat playbook) and the continuation branch's OWN classifier
#                                          # (chat-agent/turn-continuation.ts) and switch are unaffected by this flag.
# ── Deliverable hand-off (cohesive chat wave 2026-09-27, branch C — coding/deliverable-handoff.ts) ──
# A COMPLETED coding run's deliverables (files it wrote under the worktree that match the
# deliverable shapes: pdf pptx docx xlsx csv png jpg svg html md zip json — never node_modules /
# build dirs / dot-dirs / scaffold files; PRs it opened; canvases it created) are copied into the
# PARENT chat as durable chat uploads (download links the transcript already renders) and posted
# there as ONE result message (+ the shared `task` event, status done + artifacts); a top-level
# session posts on itself. Idempotent per run (store claim); never throws into finalize (≤ 20 s).
# WHO gets it (review fix, same day): the gate is LINEAGE, not the firing origin — a session whose parent is a
# HUMAN-asked chat hands off EVERY completed run with artifacts (a [HARNESS CONTINUATION] or schedule firing that
# finishes the deck in run 2+ included); a Fleet / Project Supervisor-parented lane is SKIPPED (supervisors get the
# run_completed hook; no Result rows / file copies on supervisor chats). The run_completed hook summary carries
# "[DELIVERABLES ALREADY POSTED …]" so the parent's wake acknowledges instead of re-posting. Files are copied ONE AT
# A TIME under a per-run total budget, and the whole hand-off STOPS at the 20 s deadline (AbortSignal).
# DELIVERABLE_MAX_FILES=12            # at most this many files per run (the NEWEST kept; the rest stay in the session's Files tab)
# DELIVERABLE_MAX_BYTES=26214400      # per-file cap in bytes (25 MB; never above the 25 MB ChatFile persistence cap)
# DELIVERABLE_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=52428800 # per-RUN total across every copied file (50 MB; the NEWEST that fit are kept — bounds worker memory + RDS bytea per finalize)
# DELIVERABLE_HANDOFF_SUPERVISOR_PARENTS=1 # opt-in: also post Result rows + file copies into a Fleet / Project Supervisor parent chat (default: skipped)
#                                     # (default: it is a code/docs CHANGE that rides the PR — only NEW files of those shapes are deliverables)
# DELIVERABLE_HANDOFF_ORIGIN_GATE=1   # restores the first cut's FIRING-ORIGIN gate: schedule / hook firings skipped unless …
# DELIVERABLE_HANDOFF_ALL_ORIGINS=1   # … this lifts it (meaningful only with the origin gate re-armed; the default lineage gate ignores both)
# ── Seats govern sessions (2026-09-28, branch fix/seats-govern-sessions — owner: "I changed the endpoint settings for supervisors
#    and agents in admin endpoints … many sessions didn't change"; "when I try and test laya endpoint in endpoint ui it errors") ──
# SEAT_GOVERNS_SESSIONS_DISABLED=1         # (coding/seat-governance.ts) restores the pre-fix authority: the coding_sessions.model STAMP
#                                          # governs an existing session at run time (project codingModel override → stamp) and any
#                                          # resolvable UserPreferences.codingModel — the "glm-5.2" column default every user carried
#                                          # included — counts as a personal pick at stamping time, so the admin's Workspace default
#                                          # (coding_default) seat reaches nobody. Default: ONE resolver at stamping AND run time —
#                                          # explicit session pick (spawn-param / set_session_model) → a HUMAN-set project pick
#                                          # (settings.codingModelSource 'user'; a machine-written 'machine' override never shadows
#                                          # the seat; a legacy no-provenance override applies) → a preference the user set THEMSELVES
#                                          # (context-store marker ['user',<id>,'coding-prefs']/codingModelExplicit naming the stored
#                                          # value — fail-closed; '' / "glm-5.2" are never picks) → the coding_default SEAT resolved
#                                          # live → the stamp only as the last-resort record. A NULL-provenance stamp is refreshed to
#                                          # what ran; the init event / agent input / run_spend meta carry modelSource
#                                          # ('explicit' | 'project' | 'preference' | 'seat' | 'stamp'); Account → Admin → API costs
#                                          # renders the governance split. Admin re-point: POST /admin/model-roles/apply-seats
#                                          # { dryRun } (Model roles page → "Apply seats to existing sessions", preview first;
#                                          # loop_metrics seat_apply). Migration 20260928120000 flips the column DEFAULT to '' (rows
#                                          # untouched).
#                                          # leadModel. Default: a lead-model PICK is a human decision — a scheduled / hook / agent /
#                                          # webhook turn (no user anchor, or machine-classified) is refused with no_user_turn and the
#                                          # admin's Digby seat keeps governing; clearing (null / '') and the mode half stay allowed.
#                                          # Supervisor chats never honour the column (chatLeadOverrideForRun) — unchanged.
#                                          # model. Default: a model flagged decision:'systemone_chat', kind 'decision', or on a
#                                          # decision-shaped endpoint runs ONLY the typed-decision probe (the same call /verify makes —
#                                          # capability row 'decision'); the chat probes (stream / tools / vision …) are never sent to
#                                          # it (LiteLLM → Laya answers them 500 "'coroutine' object is not an iterator") and the UI
#                                          # says "Typed-decision model — chat capabilities not applicable" instead of an error.
# ── Cohesive chat LIVE FIXES (2026-09-28, branch cohesive/live-fixes — the first live acceptance of the merged wave) ──
#                                          # HUMAN turn of a plain chat takes the user's stored codingPermissionMode as-is (a never-chosen
#                                          # pre-2026-09-17 'ask' included) and its first run is stamped origin 'agent' (machine-classified —
#                                          # in ASK mode every mutating tool AUTO-DENIES on the first call: the live defect, child 3d21b4d8).
#                                          # Default: the child is 'auto' unless the caller passed permissionMode or the user set a non-auto
#                                          # preference THEMSELVES (settings PUT / set_preferences mark it explicit in the context store), and
#                                          # its first run is USER-anchored (origin 'user' + the parent turn's userTurnAt through the first-
#                                          # prompt stash). Supervisor parents and machine turns are byte-identical to before. Telemetry:
#                                          # loop_metrics spawn_permission {childChatId, permissionMode, permissionSource, humanSpawn}.
#                                          # hand-off TARGET. Default: the result row goes to coding_messages (+ mirror) ONLY when the target
#                                          # chat has a coding session row; a PLAIN parent gets the chat row — the first cut failed on it with
#                                          # coding_messages_sessionId_fkey (parent b9ee9c20: posted:false, card stuck on running).
#                                          # run_completed / run_failed wake aimed at a HUMAN-owned NON-supervisor parent is SKIPPED at delivery
#                                          # when the hand-off POSTED for that run (summary note or store record) — rows terminal-marked
#                                          # 'skipped:handoff_posted', never replayed, gate released, no cap token, one loop_metrics
#                                          # handoff_parent_wake_skipped row; a run_failed row flips the parent's running task card to FAILED
#                                          # with the cause instead of waking (no card to flip ⇒ the wake delivers). Supervisor parents,
#                                          # attention_needed rows and an un-posted completion always deliver — the raw
#                                          # `[MACHINE-TRIGGERED RUN …]` row in a human's plain chat was the live defect.
# ── Hand-off POLISH (2026-09-28, branch backlog/handoff-polish — backlog audit CT-1 / CT-2 / CT-3 / CT-4 / E17 / DOI-09 / DOI-20) ──
#                                          # run re-copies every deliverable and posts a Result row (one top-level lane put 11 identical copies /
#                                          # 185 MB of bytea on its own chat in 11 h). Default: the id is CONTENT-keyed dh_<sha1(path:sha1(bytes))>
#                                          # so the (uploadId, chatId) ChatFile key dedupes across runs — a file whose bytes already sit on the
#                                          # target is LINKED (the Result row says "unchanged since the last hand-off"), a run whose every file is
#                                          # unchanged with no PR / canvas on a top-level self-target posts NOTHING (metric skipped:'unchanged';
#                                          # a parent target still gets its row — the completion is the news); the per-target ledger lives at
#                                          # store [deliverable-handoff, <targetChatId>] / ledger. Metric meta: deduped, pruned.
#                                          # OLDEST dh_ copies on the target that are not this run's are deleted (their earlier Result-row links go
#                                          # dead; the new row says how many were removed); never a user upload, never a file this run links.
# HANDOFF_CHAT_TOTAL_BYTES=209715200       # the per-CHAT budget over every hand-off copy on a target (200 MB)
#                                          # `/app/coding-workspaces/worktrees/<id>/deck.pdf (absolute path)` line led the row). Default: the row
#                                          # leads with **Deliverables**, then ONE paragraph with headings dropped, absolute worktree / container
#                                          # paths reduced to file names and the "(absolute path)" / "worktree" parentheticals removed (scrubSummary).
# DELETED 2026-10-30 (RSW-1 delete-with-ledger, goal 393f731e): was SPAWN_ENDS_TURN_DISABLED=1 — NF_INERT (0 compose/Dockerfile hits), reader
