# ── Dynamic roster program 2026-10-06 (owner: "drop the presets, fully agentic, any and all models"; canonical: the 2026-10-06 roster bullet in AGENTS.md) ──
# New act paths are CANARY-first (store ['instance','turn-plan']/config); each `*_DISABLED=1` restores the previous behaviour.
# Team A — depth by lanes
# (2026-10-20) the lane-depth switches below (LANE_DEPTH / LANE_CHECKER / LANE_CHECKER_POOL / LANE_FAIL_OPEN / LANE_RESEARCH_ROUTING /
# LANE_RUNGS / KEYWORD_L3_RETIRE / QUICK_PRESET_FREE, + STANDARD_LANE_THINKING_BUDGET) are the env rollback of the lane-depth flip
# (store flags laneChecker → laneFailOpen → laneResearch act fleet-wide); their release expiry is re-dated together in
# switch-registry.ts (LANE_DEPTH_ROLLBACK_SWITCHES / LANE_DEPTH_ROLLBACK_EXPIRY).
# LANE_DEPTH_DISABLED=1                       # the turn plan never sets depth (checker / fail-open / rungs) — presets decide as before
# LANE_BOARD_BLOCK_DISABLED=1                   # (2c203dac) a non-supervisor machine wake injects no lane board (linked owner questions + assigned todos) — the model recalls board state from memory
# FRAMEWORK_SIGNAL_SWEEP_DISABLED=1             # hourly DB-only framework-signal-sweep files no bug_report tickets
# FRAMEWORK_SIGNAL_DAY_CAP_DISABLED=1           # framework-signal-sweep: no per-UTC-day ticket budget (per-pass cap of 10 only) — pre-2026-10-20
# FRAMEWORK_SIGNAL_TICKETS_PER_DAY=             # framework-signal-sweep NEW tickets per UTC day across all workers (default 10; 0 = none today)
# PRODUCT_PROJECT_DOMAINS=                     # missed-bug surface routing tier 3 (ticket a2540aaa): "proj-key=domain.tld domain2.tld,other=dom3.tld" — keys are project ids (or exact names), values the product domains they serve; unset = tiers 1-2 only (chat/candidate project tokens). Opt-in: not forwarded by compose — set it in the box env deliberately.
# LANE_CHECKER_DISABLED=1                     # lane standard/checked never sets the Double Checker
# LANE_RESEARCH_ROUTING_DISABLED=1            # research routing stays the keyword router at the controller
# LANE_FAIL_OPEN_DISABLED=1                   # no "standard on the seat" lane fail-open (the preset fail-open stays)
# KEYWORD_L3_RETIRE_DISABLED=1                # a keyword Level 3 the turn plan does not call research still runs the council
# LANE_CHECKER_POOL_DISABLED=1                # a lane-checked turn uses the double_checker seat, never the checker pool
# LANE_CHECKER_FOLLOW_UP_DISABLED=1           # (2026-10-20) no follow-up hysteresis on the checker drop: a follow-up (follow_up ≥ 0.5) in a
#                                             # checked / research session may lose its checker again
# WORKSPACE_ATTACH_KIND_GATE_DISABLED=1       # (2026-10-20) a CODE_INTENT keyword hit ("fix", "bug", "merge" …) attaches a workspace again without
#                                             # asking task_kind (platform/workspace-attach-gate.ts — a confident non-code verdict keeps the chat a chat)
# USER_SPACE_CHAT_ISOLATION_DISABLED=1        # (2026-10-20) plain ungrouped chats share the hidden user-space project's memory again (its
#                                             # "[Project Context — Shared across all chats]" state + decision rows; platform/user-space.service.ts)
# LANE_RUNGS_DISABLED=1                       # Dig-deeper rungs follow the preset shapes again
# QUICK_PRESET_FREE_DISABLED=1                # Quick-lane eligibility requires preset L1/L2 again
# LANE_STANDARD_THRESHOLD=0.8                 # p(quick+standard) needed to drop the checker
# LANE_CHECKER_STAKES_CEILING=0.6             # stakes at/above this always keep the checker
# LANE_CHECKER_CONTESTED_CEILING=0.5          # contested at/above this always keeps the checker
# LANE_RESEARCH_THRESHOLD=0.5                 # p(research) as top lane to route to the council
# LANE_RESEARCH_EXPLICIT_FLOOR=0.2            # p(research) floor for an explicit keyword research request
# Team B — honest signals + retirements
