# ── Ticket dispatch + K2 fixes (2026-10-06 ticket catch-up; feedback/ticket-dispatch.service.ts; AGENTS.md "TICKET CATCH-UP" bullet) ──
# TICKET_DISPATCH_FRESH_LANES_DISABLED=1      # back to the ONE standing engineering lane (the path that parked every ticket on a busy R&D loop)
# TICKET_DISPATCH_CLOSE_RACE_DISABLED=1       # 2026-10-24 (ticket 1a6afc6a): the drain spawns without the pre-spawn status re-read — a ticket that closed between the drain's scan and its lane spawn gets its lane anyway (the dispatch/close race mishap shape: no re-read, no ticket_dispatch_close_race metric). The switch gates ONLY the drain's re-read half — the lane charters' STAND DOWN ON CLOSED clause stays in every mode (a lane standing down on an already-closed ticket is the right behavior in every mode)
# TICKET_LANE_CONCURRENCY=4                   # dedicated ticket lanes running at once (1..10)
# TICKET_LANE_CONCURRENCY_NIGHT=6             # overnight cap, 22:00–06:00 America/Vancouver (1..10)
# TICKET_LANE_NIGHT_HOURS=22-6                # night window "start-end" hours, half-open, wraps midnight
# TICKET_LANE_NO_RUN_REDISPATCH_HOURS=6       # a ticket lane with no run this long after dispatch is replaced
# TICKET_LANE_MAX_DISPATCHES=3                # lanes per ticket before auto re-dispatch stops (a reopen resets it)
# TICKET_LANE_LEGACY_REDISPATCH_DISABLED=1    # do not migrate tickets the old regime parked on the standing lane
# TICKET_LANE_FILER_GATE_DISABLED=1           # do NOT hold an agent-filed ticket for its live filer lane (the d2a1fa00 duplicate-lane race comes back)
# TICKET_LANE_ARCHIVE_PAUSE_DISABLED=1         # do NOT pause a finished lane's enabled schedules before archiving it (the bf656696 archive deadlock comes back; the 30-min stuck backstop still frees the slot)
# TICKET_LANE_ARCHIVE_GAPS_DISABLED=1          # 2026-10-21 lane-lifecycle area B: the pre-fix ticket-lane archive — closed-only take:100 / 7-day read (no awaiting_verification lanes, window starvation back), a reopen keeps the old laneArchivedAt (the next lane is never archived), a verifier-reopened ticket waits the 6 h / 8 h windows behind its archived lane, no previous-lane sweep, no heal of a satellite stuck 'running', and none of the review guards (owner-armed-schedule refusal on every automatic archive, the 6 h idle / recent-run rule for awaiting + out-of-window rows, restore-as-activity, fresh-read stamp; third review 2026-10-22: the house rules — restore marker + restore audit above all — on a closed ticket's own lane and the superseded lane at re-dispatch, remembered schedule pauses, ≤ 20 closed-lane archives / drain, ONE cascade budget per drain, the whole-window closed scan). ON for 1 / true / on (the wave's one parser)
# TICKET_LIVENESS_FAILSAFE_DISABLED=1          # a FAILED claiming-session liveness probe again counts as dead (legacy read) instead of alive-unknown fail-safe (97c06f46)
# TICKET_RECLAIM_TWO_PROBE_DISABLED=1          # a single confirmed-absent drain may reclaim a ticket again — no second-consecutive-probe requirement (97c06f46)
# TICKET_LANE_SLOT_RELEASE_DISABLED=1         # do NOT release an idle/capped lane's slot (the Oct 16-17 overnight queue stall comes back: 3/3 slots held 5h+ by sleep/deploy-poll lanes)
# TICKET_FAMILY_BATCHING_DISABLED=1           # do NOT batch auto-filer ticket families (recurring-signature/raw-marker/log-signal/tool-failure-streak) into one lane each — every family member gets its own dedicated lane again (the Oct 16-17 starvation comes back: ~24 of 40 waiting tickets were family rows)
# TICKET_FAMILY_PREFIX_V2_DISABLED=1          # TICKET-FAMILY-ROUTING (2026-10-20): only the four 47397831 families batch — incomplete-card / missed-bug (framework-signal-sweep) and av-mishap (action-verifier tickets) get a solo lane each again
# TICKET_FAMILY_PRECISION_ROUTING_DISABLED=1  # no measured-precision routing: noisy families (>= 3 of the last 5 closes false positives/siblings) are no longer filed 'queued' + limited to one family lane per UTC day, pre-fix raw-marker sightings are no longer absorbed into a merged class fix (detector-wide classes never are — they get a re-check line), and update_feedback stops stamping context.closedAt on a close (already-queued members are still drained)
# ACCEPTANCE_BASELINE_GATE_DISABLED=1         # ACCEPTANCE-METRIC-BASELINE (2026-10-20): no regex-metacharacter refusal for messagePattern and no pre-fix baseline gate (filing / close / verifier) — a metric that already passes before the fix can again reach deployed_verified vacuously
# AUTOFILER_DEFAULT_METRIC_DISABLED=1         # log-signal / raw-marker auto-filed tickets carry no default acceptance metric, and the framework_signal_finding per-finding telemetry rows stop
# TICKET_LANE_IDLE_SURRENDER_MINUTES=20       # a live lane running ONLY sleep/poll commands this long surrenders its slot (5..120; the lane keeps running)
# TICKET_LANE_SLOT_CAP_HOURS=3                # hard per-lane slot cap: a live lane dispatched longer ago than this is force-released and the Supervisor notified (0.17..24)
